{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread","id":1440062,"title":"[V5] The Sabbat thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-15T10:22:47-07:00","id":1440062,"title":"[V5] The Sabbat thread","content":"So, we're getting a Sabbat book.<br /> <br /> We have the rules for Lasombra and Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Justin Achilli is writing it.<br /> <br /> So, what do we want from this book and how will the Sabbat be portrayed from now on?<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts and hopes?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T10:56:41-07:00","id":1440070,"title":"","content":"Paths of Enlightenment being treated as serious alternates to Humanity, with a replacement of the Tenets and Touchstones systems with something that would function for them. A move away from the Revised view of the Sabbat as degenerates and idiots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 03-15-2021, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T12:34:59-07:00","id":1440089,"title":"","content":"Paths of Enlightenment. Warrior Salubri. Possibly (only just possibly) &quot;Monster Manual&quot; type entries for Kiasyd, True Brujah and other weirdies (mainly intended as one-off fights for your coterie). Probably lots of material on setting chronicles in the modern Middle East. <br /> <br /> 1:12 they try to attract the Zoomies by throwing in Abominations. Yes! This is the book where you can be a Wolfomapire!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T12:48:09-07:00","id":1440091,"title":"","content":"Didnt you already make a sabbat thread a wjile back (admitedly, it got a bit torn up by folks unhappy with the direction taken)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I would like a lasombra/tzmisce/Ravnos rewrite. <br /> paths<br /> a... how do you salvage them? pretty sure they were sent to the middle east to die. <br /> do they get awesome powers from the baali city and become an insidious boogie man for anarch kiddies?<br /> or did they never really leave their cities and just pretended to. <br /> or are they just... joining the camarilla?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T12:49:10-07:00","id":1440093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440070#post1440070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paths of Enlightenment being treated as serious alternates to Humanity, with a replacement of the Tenets and Touchstones systems with something that would function for them. A move away from the Revised view of the Sabbat as degenerates and idiots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now if they're degenerates <i>or </i>idiots. That's another thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T13:19:43-07:00","id":1440096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440093#post1440093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now if they're degenerates <i>or </i>idiots. That's another thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have been force fed the idiot ball, tis true....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T17:02:47-07:00","id":1440127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread#post1440062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what do we want from this book and how will the Sabbat be portrayed from now on?<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts and hopes?</div> </div> </div> </div>With the caveat that I don't pay much of any attention to V5:<br /> <br /> I think it would be interesting to have a Sabbat that organized itself entirely around which Path one follows rather than which clan one is descended from. Generally taking the idea that they're rebelling against the Antediluvian founders to the &quot;logical&quot; conclusion that acknowledging one's lineage makes one more vulnerable to their manipulations and control. So, &quot;anti-tribe&quot; takes on a new meaning, as they reject clan ties in favor of those formed with fellow Road practitioners. Also, in the case of Packs, the Pack Priest would be the one who is the most advanced in their understanding the single Path the entire Pack follows. <br /> <br /> I've no idea if this would be at all feasible under V5, but I just think it would be interesting. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T17:31:14-07:00","id":1440130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440127#post1440127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be interesting to have a Sabbat that organized itself entirely around which Path one follows rather than which clan one is descended from. Generally taking the idea that they're rebelling against the Antediluvian founders to the &quot;logical&quot; conclusion that acknowledging one's lineage makes one more vulnerable to their manipulations and control. So, &quot;anti-tribe&quot; takes on a new meaning, as they reject clan ties in favor of those formed with fellow Road practitioners. Also, in the case of Packs, the Pack Priest would be the one who is the most advanced in their understanding the single Path the entire Pack follows.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's an interesting take, and I kind of already do that with Sabbat NPCs in my chronicles. It makes sense for many packs to be based around the same Path of Enlightenment especially since any &quot;priest&quot; is realistically unlikely to be able to support a multitude of paths.<br /> <br /> (Also, in my chronicles the pack priest reports to the Bishops, and that often makes them a kind of political commissar in service to the ambitious bishops who are primarily Lasombra and Tzimisce centralizers of the sect, so it creates political tension between the ductus and priest.)<br /> <br /> Of course, this doesn't mean that a Sabbat &quot;organized&quot; around Paths means that all packs are build around them. As much as I think that makes sense, it makes for a poor game for PCs. Picking your own Path of Enlightenment is very much an individual PC choice like picking a clan. It's rare for all the PCs to pick the same path. So you need to portray the sect in such a way that multi-path Sabbat packs are still normal and unremarkable.<br /> <br /> So I agree with you that there should be less of a clan-based organization within the Sabbat. Not something entirely eliminated, and there would be strong factions inside it which were clan based (including factions seemingly based around Paths which are actually a vehicle for one of the clans - primarily the Lasombra and Tzimisce). In fact, I think a lot of the original fighters of the Anarch Revolt would be most opposed to real clan structures within the Sabbat since they would recognize them as tools of the elders. For example, it would be a great way to distinguish those &quot;young&quot; Lasombra of the Anarch Revolt truly committed to destroying the elders and liberating all vampires, and the &quot;elder&quot; Lasombra who only joined the sect out of expedience and a belief that it was a better route to power through them than with the Camarilla. It never made sense for me that the former Lasombra Anarchs would retain something like the Courts of the Blood. That made more sense as something secretly retained by the Lasombra anti-tribu in the Camarilla, and as among a dark secret of the elders who joined the Sabbat quite late or out of ambition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 03-16-2021, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T20:41:52-07:00","id":1440138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440127#post1440127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the caveat that I don't pay much of any attention to V5:<br /> <br /> I think it would be interesting to have a Sabbat that organized itself entirely around which Path one follows rather than which clan one is descended from. Generally taking the idea that they're rebelling against the Antediluvian founders to the &quot;logical&quot; conclusion that acknowledging one's lineage makes one more vulnerable to their manipulations and control. So, &quot;anti-tribe&quot; takes on a new meaning, as they reject clan ties in favor of those formed with fellow Road practitioners. Also, in the case of Packs, the Pack Priest would be the one who is the most advanced in their understanding the single Path the entire Pack follows.<br /> <br /> I've no idea if this would be at all feasible under V5, but I just think it would be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an extremely cool idea and makes a ton of sense to me, though I would go with the idea that there are &quot;pure&quot; packs and &quot;mixed&quot; some with vampires who all share a single path and some with vampires from different paths (which are more likely to be player character packs, since most likely each player might prefer to follow a different path).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T22:55:09-07:00","id":1440143,"title":"","content":"I am hoping that THE SABBAT book will continue the trend of being primarily fiction based but I am also hoping that it will have plenty of rules information as well. I want the sense of what the Sabbat is up to and I want them to roll back SOME of the changes for 5th Edition but not all of them. I am admittedly primarily a lore junkie and the rules have always been less important to me than the specifics of rules.<br /> <br /> Still, if I wanted to say what I wanted from the book, here's my list:<br /> <br /> * An in-character story about the Fall of Mexico City<br /> * An in-character story about the Fall of Montreal<br /> * An in-character story about the Lasombra Defection<br /> * The current status of the Lasombra Loyalists<br /> * A basic sense of how many ancients and Elders were killed by the Sabbat during the Gehenna Crusade [This sounds silly but if the Sabbat were supposed to be on this Crusade and getting their asses kicked, I'd like them to have actually inflicted massive damage on the number of Camarilla Beckoned and monsters awakened--give back the Sabbat some dignity]<br /> * The return of House Goratrix<br /> * The fate of Lucita (I swear she's not my waifu....that's Victoria Ash)<br /> * The Drowned Legacies vs. The Sabbat<br /> * Who the current Regents or Regents are<br /> * How many Sabbat defected to the Anarchs and Church of Caine<br /> <br /> I'd like to also to have some modified Humanity rules. It doesn't have to be extensive but at least the following:<br /> <br /> * Sabbat do not suffer Stains for killing or torturing humans.<br /> * Sabbat can have fellow vampires as their Touchstones like members of their Pack<br /> <br /> Basically, I'd like the Sabbat to return from the Gehenna Crusade but with a trade off of having lost some major cities but also having severely reduced the number of Elders and Methuselahs in the world.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://media.tenor.com/images/8d8d837fca3d687d53826e5202537af5/tenor.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T23:02:18-07:00","id":1440146,"title":"","content":"Part of what I want is simply for the Long Road Out Of Hell to become canon: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N7z5WJa4WcghanB-mSGqdqIymRB7vteu/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N7z...ymRB7vteu/view</a><br /> I love how that fan-made supplement does Paths, and it would please me greatly to have it simply adopted.<br /> <br /> The other thing is I want the Sabbat to have their own cities again. I'm not interested in them only infiltrators in Cammy cities. The Sabbat are the default sect in my games. I have zero interest in them simply being the boogeymen to a sect who barely ever even show up in my games. The Sabbat are not Nephandi or Baali. The Sabbat are their own distinct, complex culture and work just fine interacting almost exclusively with each other and mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T23:09:34-07:00","id":1440148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440146#post1440146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of what I want is simply for the Long Road Out Of Hell to become canon: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N7z5WJa4WcghanB-mSGqdqIymRB7vteu/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N7z...ymRB7vteu/view</a><br /> I love how that fan-made supplement does Paths, and it would please me greatly to have it simply adopted.<br /> <br /> The other thing is I want the Sabbat to have their own cities again. I'm not interested in them only infiltrators in Cammy cities. The Sabbat are the default sect in my games. I have zero interest in them simply being the boogeymen to a sect who barely ever even show up in my games. The Sabbat are not Nephandi or Baali. The Sabbat are their own distinct, complex culture and work just fine interacting almost exclusively with each other and mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Am I alone in wanting the Path of Evil Revelations to be an accepted part of the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> Or at least powerful enough to openly feud with the Inquisition?<br /> <br /> Those guys deserve some respect!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T23:12:10-07:00","id":1440149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440138#post1440138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an extremely cool idea and makes a ton of sense to me, though I would go with the idea that there are &quot;pure&quot; packs and &quot;mixed&quot; some with vampires who all share a single path and some with vampires from different paths (which are more likely to be player character packs, since most likely each player might prefer to follow a different path).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been pondering the idea that, when an attack on a city fails, survivors of decimated packs get shoved together for a bit, seeing if they learn to coexist, convert each other or go their separate ways when they reach a Sabbat held city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T23:25:44-07:00","id":1440153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440148#post1440148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Am I alone in wanting the Path of Evil Revelations to be an accepted part of the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> Or at least powerful enough to openly feud with the Inquisition?<br /> <br /> Those guys deserve some respect!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'd say you are pretty much alone in that desire, or at least your desire is only shared by those who think of the Sabbat as simply something for Cammies to punch.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T23:32:39-07:00","id":1440154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440153#post1440153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I'd say you are pretty much alone in that desire, or at least your desire is only shared by those who think of the Sabbat as simply something for Cammies to punch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is funny because my love for the Path of Evil Revelations is from my Sabbat games.<br /> <br /> You need someone for the Sabbat to punch other than the Cammies.<br /> <br /> The Evil Revelations people add an internal enemy to fight and an ideological challenge to the Paths.<br /> <br /> &quot;What makes us worse?&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> The Sabbat as a force willing to wield the power of Hell against the Antediluvians isn't an argument that I think is necessarily a bad one. After all, the infernal is a weapon and we have Demon: The Fallen. Sure, most of them are pure evil but what IS evil? The other Sabbat may argue that it is against freedom (but are they free) or that the forces of Hell are even worse than the Antediluvians but the Road of the Devil was actually a fairly moral (comparatively) group during the Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> What separates the Damned from the damned?<br /> <br /> I'm interested in those kind of questions.<br /> <br /> Then again, I tend to think of the Nephandi as more interesting than the Union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-16-2021, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T01:16:18-07:00","id":1440160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440148#post1440148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I alone in wanting the Path of Evil Revelations to be an accepted part of the Sabbat?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You need someone for the Sabbat to punch other than the Cammies. </div> </div> </div>These two sentiments seem to be in conflict, at least on the face of it. The Path of Evil Revelations was always meant to be the worm at the core of the Sabbat, but I don't think it should ever be an <i>accepted</i> or <i>respected</i> part of the sect. Infernalists working in secret already fulfil the function of an internal enemy for the Sabbat to fight. I'm not sure what an Infernalist faction that openly declared themselves would add to the sect. They pose no ideological challenge to the other Paths of Enlightenment, because the Path of Evil Revelations is the path of pure slavery to Infernal masters. That fact alone ensures that no Sabbat vampire who wasn't already an Infernalist would take even two seconds to consider their argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T02:05:08-07:00","id":1440167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440143#post1440143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am hoping that THE SABBAT book will continue the trend of being primarily fiction based but I am also hoping that it will have plenty of rules information as well. I want the sense of what the Sabbat is up to and I want them to roll back SOME of the changes for 5th Edition but not all of them. I am admittedly primarily a lore junkie and the rules have always been less important to me than the specifics of rules.<br /> <br /> Still, if I wanted to say what I wanted from the book, here's my list:<br /> <br /> * An in-character story about the Fall of Mexico City<br /> * An in-character story about the Fall of Montreal<br /> * An in-character story about the Lasombra Defection<br /> * The current status of the Lasombra Loyalists<br /> * A basic sense of how many ancients and Elders were killed by the Sabbat during the Gehenna Crusade [This sounds silly but if the Sabbat were supposed to be on this Crusade and getting their asses kicked, I'd like them to have actually inflicted massive damage on the number of Camarilla Beckoned and monsters awakened--give back the Sabbat some dignity]<br /> * The return of House Goratrix<br /> * The fate of Lucita (I swear she's not my waifu....that's Victoria Ash)<br /> * The Drowned Legacies vs. The Sabbat<br /> * Who the current Regents or Regents are<br /> * How many Sabbat defected to the Anarchs and Church of Caine<br /> <br /> I'd like to also to have some modified Humanity rules. It doesn't have to be extensive but at least the following:<br /> <br /> * Sabbat do not suffer Stains for killing or torturing humans.<br /> * Sabbat can have fellow vampires as their Touchstones like members of their Pack<br /> <br /> Basically, I'd like the Sabbat to return from the Gehenna Crusade but with a trade off of having lost some major cities but also having severely reduced the number of Elders and Methuselahs in the world.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://media.tenor.com/images/8d8d837fca3d687d53826e5202537af5/tenor.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>I could go with this take on V5 Sabbat. It would bring my table back to the game, as we play Sabbat by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T04:13:26-07:00","id":1440178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440160#post1440160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These two sentiments seem to be in conflict, at least on the face of it. The Path of Evil Revelations was always meant to be the worm at the core of the Sabbat, but I don't think it should ever be an <i>accepted</i> or <i>respected</i> part of the sect. Infernalists working in secret already fulfil the function of an internal enemy for the Sabbat to fight. I'm not sure what an Infernalist faction that openly declared themselves would add to the sect. They pose no ideological challenge to the other Paths of Enlightenment, because the Path of Evil Revelations is the path of pure slavery to Infernal masters. That fact alone ensures that no Sabbat vampire who wasn't already an Infernalist would take even two seconds to consider their argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, my reasoning is that sensible players would oppose the Path of Evil Revelations gaining strength within the sect and trying to become the default measure of the sect. It would be an attempt to prevent their sect from sliding into becoming the Beast-ruled caricature that so many Sabbat players loathe. In my own Sabbat games, one of the central conflicts is the fact that the Path of Enlightenment followers hated that the sect was slowly transforming into the theme park version of itself due to mass Embraces and lack of spirituality.<br /> <br /> A focus on conquering territory and War parties over achieving a higher inhuman morality.<br /> <br /> My Technocrat games are similar where the PCs struggle against the worst of their sect as part of the central conflict. In this case, the Path of Evil Revelations nad its members have grown so numerous and gained so many recruits that it is now a central part and rooting it out is more difficult than ever.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-16-2021, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T05:45:07-07:00","id":1440186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440148#post1440148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Am I alone in wanting the Path of Evil Revelations to be an accepted part of the Sabbat?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be interesting to see the Path expanded/diversified, perhaps in ways similar to Belial's Brood in Requiem. I'm not 100% sure I want that as part of the Sabbat, but I'm not 100% against it either. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T06:24:21-07:00","id":1440192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440143#post1440143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">:<br /> <br /> 1)* Sabbat do not suffer Stains for killing or torturing humans.<br /> * Sabbat can have fellow vampires as their Touchstones like members of their Pack<br /> <br /> Basically, I'd like the Sabbat to return from the Gehenna Crusade but with a trade off of having lost some major cities but also having severely reduced the number of Elders and Methuselahs in the world.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://media.tenor.com/images/8d8d837fca3d687d53826e5202537af5/tenor.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>1) Doesn't work, gives a totally different play experience from Paths, and feels nothing like the Sabbat. At least in the testing I have taken part in. We tried: Ignoring Morality entirely, so it was just RP, but that didn't have teeth, and felt hollow. Vampires or Ritae as Touchstones, with Chronicle Tenets, which didn't make sense, the Paths don't care about the same things, and what would cause degeneration to one is not even considered worthy of note by another, let alone something that needs 'mitigation' via touchstone, and a few variations on both. Basically Tenets undermine the concept, and Touchstones don't make sense as an external force, Paths are 100% internal weapons against the beast, having them tied to anything else but will and intellect makes them hollow shadows, Ritae where the least bad for this, because at least then you could argue that Power and the Inner Voices meditation counted, or the research of the Noddists, or the Hunts of Feral Heart or Orion, but even then...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T06:26:47-07:00","id":1440193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440148#post1440148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Am I alone in wanting the Path of Evil Revelations to be an accepted part of the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> Or at least powerful enough to openly feud with the Inquisition?<br /> <br /> Those guys deserve some respect!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, because of what it is, a knew set of masters, as bad or worse than the Antes. Having the Infernalists and Baali running thru all sects, and clans, like a malignant spiritual plague could and should be played up however. A demon has as much to offer a Prince as a pauper after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T07:07:33-07:00","id":1440197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440148#post1440148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Am I alone in wanting the Path of Evil Revelations to be an accepted part of the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> Or at least powerful enough to openly feud with the Inquisition?<br /> <br /> Those guys deserve some respect!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Evil Revelations violates spirit of the sabbat because you enslave yourself to another. <br /> <br /> Now something like Howl of the Devil Tiger style demonologists who make demons their bitches and do horrible things to get ahead. Maybe Something like a PIV Demonologist branch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T12:43:06-07:00","id":1440234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440192#post1440192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) Doesn't work, gives a totally different play experience from Paths, and feels nothing like the Sabbat. At least in the testing I have taken part in. We tried: Ignoring Morality entirely, so it was just RP, but that didn't have teeth, and felt hollow. Vampires or Ritae as Touchstones, with Chronicle Tenets, which didn't make sense, the Paths don't care about the same things, and what would cause degeneration to one is not even considered worthy of note by another, let alone something that needs 'mitigation' via touchstone, and a few variations on both. Basically Tenets undermine the concept, and Touchstones don't make sense as an external force, Paths are 100% internal weapons against the beast, having them tied to anything else but will and intellect makes them hollow shadows, Ritae where the least bad for this, because at least then you could argue that Power and the Inner Voices meditation counted, or the research of the Noddists, or the Hunts of Feral Heart or Orion, but even then...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Path of Evil Revelations isn't without morality. Otherwise it wouldn't hold the Beast at bay. It is just a morality of Hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T12:54:52-07:00","id":1440237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440127#post1440127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">With the caveat that I don't pay much of any attention to V5:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think it would be interesting to have a Sabbat that organized itself entirely around which Path one follows rather than which clan one is descended from. Generally taking the idea that they're rebelling against the Antediluvian founders to the &quot;logical&quot; conclusion that acknowledging one's lineage makes one more vulnerable to their manipulations and control. So, &quot;anti-tribe&quot; takes on a new meaning, as they reject clan ties in favor of those formed with fellow Road practitioners. Also, in the case of Packs, the Pack Priest would be the one who is the most advanced in their understanding the single Path the entire Pack follows.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I've no idea if this would be at all feasible under V5, but I just think it would be interesting.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that this is a really neat idea! But I also agree with the others who have argued that their needs to be room for Packs consisting of multiple Paths, especially if you want PCs forming a Pack together. Following up on your idea about the Priest of a single-Path Pack being a spiritual guide in that particular Path, I was thinking that the role of a Priest in a multi-Path Pack might be more focused on finding the ways that the different philosophies of the various Paths represented can be formed into a collective philosophy or purpose for the Pack itself, an ideological bridge connecting the different Paths of the group.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> the post you just quoted wasn't talking about PoER, it was referring to your previous suggestion that violence against humans wouldn't cause Stains for Sabbat characters. People's criticism of Evil Revelations doesn't seem to be about morality, per se, but autonomy; they see the Sabbat as fundamentally committed to freedom from supernatural 'Hidden Masters,' while the PoER is centred on worshipping a sort of 'Hidden Master.' Their position seems to be that such a group functions well as a hidden 'enemy within,' but the ideological clash with the principles of the Sabbat as a group doesn't leave much room for them as a publicly accepted part of the group. Not my area of expertise, so I can't add much, just figured I'd make sure people aren't talking past each other by accident <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 03-16-2021, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T12:58:13-07:00","id":1440238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440234#post1440234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Path of Evil Revelations isn't without morality. Otherwise it wouldn't hold the Beast at bay. It is just a morality of Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> how is that, in any way, related to what I wrote?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T13:12:36-07:00","id":1440242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440238#post1440238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> how is that, in any way, related to what I wrote?</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad. I misunderstood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The post you just quoted wasn't talking about PoER, it was referring to your previous suggestion that violence against humans wouldn't cause Stains for Sabbat characters. People's criticism of Evil Revelations doesn't seem to be about morality, per se, but autonomy; they see the Sabbat as fundamentally committed to freedom from supernatural 'Hidden Masters,' while the PoER is centred on worshipping a sort of 'Hidden Master.' Their position seems to be that such a group functions well as a hidden 'enemy within,' but the ideological clash with the principles of the Sabbat as a group doesn't leave much room for them as a publicly accepted part of the group. Not my area of expertise, so I can't add much, just figured I'd make sure people aren't talking past each other by accident </div> </div> </div>1. Violence against humans doesn't hurt the Sabbat because it's not a crime. They should lose morality for actions against OTHER vampires. Killing a human or torturing them is not something that the Sabbat cares about. Whether they do it for food or fun, the culture of the Sabbat reinforces that human lives are valueleless.<br /> <br /> Human head football is not an aversion of the Path but an expression of their contempt for the kine.<br /> <br /> 2. The Armies of Hell are fighting for freedom as well. The Sabbat are not honestly any freerer than them and I think that as an argument isn't a terrible one. Mind you, I may just want the Path of Evil Revelations to be expanded beyond cariacture. Some people had a problem with the Baali being moved from, &quot;We are servants of Hell, bwahhaha&quot; to &quot;We are keeping the Great Old Ones asleep&quot; but I always felt it was a really good update and very interesting.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat without infernalists is just a lesser organization for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-16-2021, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T13:17:37-07:00","id":1440243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440197#post1440197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Evil Revelations violates spirit of the sabbat because you enslave yourself to another.<br /> <br /> Now something like Howl of the Devil Tiger style demonologists who make demons their bitches and do horrible things to get ahead. Maybe Something like a PIV Demonologist branch?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the Luciferian Satanism/Milton's Paradise Lost angle, which would probably work with the Sabbat. I'd have to dig out my copy of ... the 2nd ed Sabbat Storyteller Handbook, I think? to see how compatible with PoER that would be. It could also work as an aspect of Power &amp; Inner Voice, maybe? IIRC the version of the Path of Night from the revised Lasombra book also draws on some of the same ideas as Devil Tiger. I think the Cainite Heresy book for Dark Ages also had some discussion about the Path of Evil Revelations being used in unconventional ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T13:20:29-07:00","id":1440245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440243#post1440243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's the Luciferian Satanism/Milton's Paradise Lost angle, which would probably work with the Sabbat. I'd have to dig out my copy of ... the 2nd ed Sabbat Storyteller Handbook, I think? to see how compatible with PoER that would be. It could also work as an aspect of Power &amp; Inner Voice, maybe? IIRC the version of the Path of Night from the revised Lasombra book also draws on some of the same ideas as Devil Tiger. I think the Cainite Heresy book for Dark Ages also had some discussion about the Path of Evil Revelations being used in unconventional ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Devil Tigers or &quot;simply uses Infernalism for power&quot; would be more what I was thinking.<br /> <br /> Either that or a somewhat more moral version like the Road of the Devil where the Devil is a way to break free from society's exceptations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T13:29:34-07:00","id":1440252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440242#post1440242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's literally a response to the first sentence you wrote: &quot;1) Doesn't work, gives a totally different play experience from Paths, and feels nothing like the Sabbat.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 1. Violence against humans doesn't hurt the Sabbat because it's not a crime. They should lose morality for actions against OTHER vampires. Killing a human or torturing them is not something that the Sabbat cares about. Whether they do it for food or fun, the culture of the Sabbat reinforces that human lives are valueleless.<br /> <br /> Human head football is not an aversion of the Path but an expression of their contempt for the kine.<br /> <br /> 2. The Armies of Hell are fighting for freedom as well. The Sabbat are not honestly any freerer than them and I think that as an argument isn't a terrible one. Mind you, I may just want the Path of Evil Revelations to be expanded beyond cariacture. Some people had a problem with the Baali being moved from, &quot;We are servants of Hell, bwahhaha&quot; to &quot;We are keeping the Great Old Ones asleep&quot; but I always felt it was a really good update and very interesting.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat without infernalists is just a lesser organization for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which was in reference to the part of your post I have put 1) next to that being *Sabbat do not suffer stains for torturing and killing humans. That was what I was responding to.<br /> <br /> Anyway: 1) Depends on the Path, Nocturnal Redemption would care about abusing humans, Caine wouldn't. You cannot make sweeping rules for the Sabbat like that, because you run into the same problem as with Tenets: The paths do not agree on enough, morality is deeply personal, it isn't defined, or aided in anyway by anything outside the person holding those convictions. Morality pets don't work, repetitive actions don't work, rituals don't work it is totally and purely, conviction and intellect vs the beast.<br /> <br /> 2) they are fighting for their freedom, and to enslave humanity and supernaturals as faith batteries (mostly varies with DtF faction, and even then this means we are stuck with DtF Demons, not the cthonic weirdness of the Nephandic demons, who are far more interesting.) Claiming they are freedom fighters is like claiming the Antes are, they are both fighting for their own freedom and food. <br /> <br /> Infernalists should be a universal problem, not a Sabbat only problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T13:31:34-07:00","id":1440253,"title":"","content":"A random thought: Given the Path of Evil Revelations' name, coupled with how DA:V made it a sub-path for the Road of Sin (which somewhat orriented toward keeping the Beast distracted or overloaded), I think it might be potentially interesting if the Path was based (originally?) on the idea of learning forbidden truths about the world so terrible that they stun the Beast into silence and stupor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T13:54:35-07:00","id":1440256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440253#post1440253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A random thought: Given the Path of Evil Revelations' name, coupled with how DA:V made it a sub-path for the Road of Sin (which somewhat orriented toward keeping the Beast distracted or overloaded), I think it might be potentially interesting if the Path was based (originally?) on the idea of learning forbidden truths about the world so terrible that they stun the Beast into silence and stupor.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Road of Sin Paths could fit very well, my guess is Evil Rev is Path of Screams by another name, but ymmv <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T14:02:59-07:00","id":1440258,"title":"","content":"Generally, I think the biggest issue that the Sabbat should have when updated for 5E is that the central conflict between the sects and Jyhad is something that should be strongly eased back from. The whole Eastern Coast being consumed with war resulted in the Anarchs vs. Camarilla, Camarilla vs. Camarilla, and Anarchs vs. Anarchs plots getting thrown out.<br /> <br /> As such, having a lot of internal conflicts to occupy the Sword of Caine seems like it would be something very important to deal with as well as questions about how to deal with the Second Inquisition as well as aftermath of the Gehenna War.<br /> <br /> <b>1:] The Infernalists are a rising power</b><br /> <br /> The idea of the Infernalists now being so well-embedded in the Sabbat and their power so strong was a suggestion not for player characters, even if I've enjoyed a good Demon: The Fallen game, but because they show the kind of corruption that devoted Sabbat players might want to confront within their ranks. Also, yes, &quot;how much different am I really?&quot; I also think that player characters who DO have their souls still but have Dark Blood Sorcery should be viable player options as well.<br /> <br /> <b>2:] Those Lost to the Beast</b><br /> <br /> This is ripping off my own campaign but my Elder Sabbat game had the idea that the 1999 Sabbat Crusade resulted in vast numbers of shovelheads being created that ended up becoming large enough to be a force themselves. Also, with the loss of groups like the Tremere Antitribu and Path of Harmony, these Low Humanity psychopath Sabbat warped the Sword of Caine from its mystic roots and were the cariactured version of Sabbat. Just the mindless diablerie-addicted psychopath Sabbat that reveled in evil for its own sake. And the Sabbat couldn't control them.<br /> <br /> <b>3. Equalizing the Power Structure</b><br /> <br /> With the Lasombra having so many defections and whatever is going on with the Tzimsice, it's interesting to speculate that the Sabbat may no longer be &quot;two clans plus the Antitribu&quot; but now actually something that is a sect where everyone is more or less equal in power structure. It causes a lot of interesting questions about what everyone is actually fighting for. Certainly, the largest argument for the Sabbat's leaders were, &quot;We destroyed our Antediluvian!&quot; Except, we know both Lasombra and Tzimisce are alive and probably the Sabbat do too now.<br /> <br /> <b>4. Reborn Ancients</b><br /> <br /> The Tal'Mah'Re are kind of a concept that I hesitate to bring back but if you were going to do it then having a bunch of Monty Covens where ancient Kindred Methuselahs have possessed younger vampires and started rebuilding it seems to be a place where you could do it. They would be a poison in the heart of the Sabbat, corrupting it from the inside into a weapon against their enemies and in the service of the Ancients.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T14:12:44-07:00","id":1440260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440258#post1440258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, I think the biggest issue that the Sabbat should have when updated for 5E is that the central conflict between the sects and Jyhad is something that should be strongly eased back from. The whole Eastern Coast being consumed with war resulted in the Anarchs vs. Camarilla, Camarilla vs. Camarilla, and Anarchs vs. Anarchs plots getting thrown out.<br /> <br /> As such, having a lot of internal conflicts to occupy the Sword of Caine seems like it would be something very important to deal with as well as questions about how to deal with the Second Inquisition as well as aftermath of the Gehenna War.<br /> <br /> <b>1:] The Infernalists are a rising power</b><br /> <br /> The idea of the Infernalists now being so well-embedded in the Sabbat and their power so strong was a suggestion not for player characters, even if I've enjoyed a good Demon: The Fallen game, but because they show the kind of corruption that devoted Sabbat players might want to confront within their ranks. Also, yes, &quot;how much different am I really?&quot; I also think that player characters who DO have their souls still but have Dark Blood Sorcery should be viable player options as well.<br /> <br /> <b>2:] Those Lost to the Beast</b><br /> <br /> This is ripping off my own campaign but my Elder Sabbat game had the idea that the 1999 Sabbat Crusade resulted in vast numbers of shovelheads being created that ended up becoming large enough to be a force themselves. Also, with the loss of groups like the Tremere Antitribu and Path of Harmony, these Low Humanity psychopath Sabbat warped the Sword of Caine from its mystic roots and were the cariactured version of Sabbat. Just the mindless diablerie-addicted psychopath Sabbat that reveled in evil for its own sake. And the Sabbat couldn't control them.<br /> <br /> <b>3. Equalizing the Power Structure</b><br /> <br /> With the Lasombra having so many defections and whatever is going on with the Tzimsice, it's interesting to speculate that the Sabbat may no longer be &quot;two clans plus the Antitribu&quot; but now actually something that is a sect where everyone is more or less equal in power structure. It causes a lot of interesting questions about what everyone is actually fighting for. Certainly, the largest argument for the Sabbat's leaders were, &quot;We destroyed our Antediluvian!&quot; Except, we know both Lasombra and Tzimisce are alive and probably the Sabbat do too now.<br /> <br /> <b>4. Reborn Ancients</b><br /> <br /> The Tal'Mah'Re are kind of a concept that I hesitate to bring back but if you were going to do it then having a bunch of Monty Covens where ancient Kindred Methuselahs have possessed younger vampires and started rebuilding it seems to be a place where you could do it. They would be a poison in the heart of the Sabbat, corrupting it from the inside into a weapon against their enemies and in the service of the Ancients.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1) Only if they are a universally rising power. having them in the Sabbat as a target for the Inquisition (or really something the Inquisition use as an excuse for sect politics) apart from in places with a definite reason for it is weird because Infernalism is as valuable, if not more so, to the other sects, and they don't look for it, having the Lasombra defection being a cover for the Angellis Ater to break away, both to escape the Inquisition, and to infest the other sects, who do not even believe they are real, would go along way to making that move make more sense.<br /> <br /> 2) Purging mindless shovelheads could be an interesting right of passage (or rounding them up, shipping them out, and throwing them at Anarch cities....<br /> <br /> 3) Ok, probably honestly have the Paths rise as a rival structure, just as they were in the Dark Ages. <br /> <br /> 4) Don't bring back the Tal'Mah'Re, have a mix of Inconnu infiltrators (because who ever actually believed they just watched) and Monty Covens, other wise we will have..what? 4 posions at the heart of the Sabbat, as opposed to the 0 in the other sects.... and then they just become butt monkeys and failures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T14:15:46-07:00","id":1440262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--g