ching the Road of Blood to non-Assamites.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is interesting a diab heavy path is built around a book that pretty much says diab is the worst thing ever...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T13:00:07-07:00","id":1440380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440378#post1440378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is interesting a diab heavy path is built around a book that pretty much says diab is the worst thing ever...</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as a religious person, that is probably the most realistic religious element of the Cainite faith.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T14:52:31-07:00","id":1440386,"title":"","content":"Unless you plan to run games exclusively in the Middle East, we'll need some attention to the &quot;remnant&quot; Sabbat setup in Europe and the Americas - who are they, what type(s) of Sabbat rejected the call to crusade, how are they organized?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T14:57:39-07:00","id":1440387,"title":"","content":"Most likely, they'd be those Sabbat who simply want to quietly progress on their paths, and never gave much of a damn about the Antes to begin with. To them, the Camarilla is ridiculous because it insists on everyone pretending to be a member of a different species, and Anarchs are just Cammies with the serial numbers filled off.<br /> <br /> Indeed, I think they might especially not care about the Antes now that &quot;Gehenna&quot; has been revealed to be so much smaller than the cataclysmic most were envisioning. THAT'S what everyone was afraid of? Here's an idea, just let the Antes play in the middle east, while we devote eternity to spiritual advancement along our chosen paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 03-17-2021, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T15:35:13-07:00","id":1440392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440387#post1440387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most likely, they'd be those Sabbat who simply want to quietly progress on their paths, and never gave much of a damn about the Antes to begin with. To them, the Camarilla is ridiculous because it insists on everyone pretending to be a member of a different species, and Anarchs are just Cammies with the serial numbers filled off.<br /> <br /> <b>Indeed, I think they might especially not care about the Antes now that &quot;Gehenna&quot; has been revealed to be so much smaller than the cataclysmic most were envisioning. THAT'S what everyone was afraid of? Here's an idea, just let the Antes play in the middle east, while we devote eternity to spiritual advancement along our chosen paths.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that the latter will be true because the Sabbat were on the front lines of it, serving as the knife and fork for the Antedilluvians slicing up and eating their meal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T23:23:53-07:00","id":1440411,"title":"","content":"For as long as I remember myself playing Vampire, we always did it very supernatural light, street level, personal problems type of game, when meeting another kindred was a really big deal for the PCs, and the world kinda felt lonely and unknown. This is why we never went for the Sabbat because it always felt like more combat, murder-hobo, action type of scenario (I am not saying that it's really is like that though). It's just that I think when you in a way accept that you are a monster a lot of the drama and the self-conflict is removed from the game, and we found characters with paths very unrelatable.<br /> <br /> So I would really like it if there would be a way to play Sabbat but still experience internal conflict, and personal horror, and fearing of losing things you care about and all that. Again, I am not talking from experience, and I would love it if people who played Sabbat can explain more what the game is about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24461,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24461-godforsaken","user":"Godforsaken","date":". 03-18-2021, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24461-godforsaken","name":"Godforsaken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-17T23:38:40-07:00","id":1440413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godforsaken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440411#post1440411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I would really like it if there would be a way to play Sabbat but still experience internal conflict, and personal horror, and fearing of losing things you care about and all that. Again, I am not talking from experience, and I would love it if people who played Sabbat can explain more what the game is about.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the funny things is that a lot of people think that the Sabbat are a group I don't like when they're easily my second favorite sect in the game. The Anarchs edge them out but only by a little.<br /> <br /> I think the primary appeal of the Sabbat is the divorce from the human element of the game and the focus on the vampire element of the game, which doesn't mean that your characters are less likely to have friends, fall in love, be willing to die for one person, or have deep emotional torment. Essentially, it's just that your &quot;side&quot; is now your fellow vampires and all the people that you are invested in are among the Damned.<br /> <br /> I actually don't play the Sabbat as fundamentally that different from the Garou, which is an interesting parallel that I think fans of both might object to. The Sabbat KNOW that the world is under the control of the Antediluvians and the Camarilla is a disease that is going to rot them all out so you need to fight the latter to fight the former. However, that war is complicated by all manner of internal politics, weird spirituality, and infighting as well as people who only get the CAINITE MYTHOLOGY FOR DUMMIES version of your religion.<br /> <br /> One of my favorite conversations in-game was about, of all things, love. The Sabbat leader said that if he did love any of the people in his mortal life then he should change them. If he doesn't then ask, &quot;Why are you willing to see them age, rot, and die? When you can instead love them for eternity.&quot;<br /> <br /> Said romantic elder also committed suicide because his partner for centuries died. It was all very tragic.<br /> <br /> Another bit was where a Sabbat Elder basically said that he hated &quot;human head soccer&quot;, fleshcrafted furniture, and torturing mortals because it was so...silly. It was like humans going out and torturing animals. It was beneath the dignity of Sabbat. He gladly killed humans for a meal and didn't hesitate to kill to protect their secrets or for resources but the sadism against them was just a reflection of what he considered to be lingering Humanity. The Sabbat don't romanticize humans or Humanity--the worst elements of Kindred society are the same as mortals so why pretend they're better?<br /> <br /> Sabbat aren't just inhuman, they are POST-HUMAN and have their own morality, beliefs, culture, and religion that focuses on different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-18-2021, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T00:16:34-07:00","id":1440416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440413#post1440413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually don't play the Sabbat as fundamentally that different from the Garou, which is an interesting parallel that I think fans of both might object to. The Sabbat KNOW that the world is under the control of the Antediluvians and the Camarilla is a disease that is going to rot them all out so you need to fight the latter to fight the former. However, that war is complicated by all manner of internal politics, weird spirituality, and infighting as well as people who only get the CAINITE MYTHOLOGY FOR DUMMIES version of your religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>In hindsight, I lament that the Paths of Enlightenment never got &quot;clanbook&quot; style books that went in depth about what they believe and ways to play them, including several premade character template illistrating this.<br /> <br /> Weirdly, one of the more useful Path of Metamorphosis sources ended up being the Ordo Dracul book for Requiem.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T00:31:58-07:00","id":1440417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440416#post1440416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In hindsight, I lament that the Paths of Enlightenment never got &quot;clanbook&quot; style books that went in depth about what they believe and ways to play them, including several premade character template illistrating this.<br /> <br /> Weirdly, one of the more useful Path of Metamorphosis sources ended up being the Ordo Dracul book for Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the funny things is I actually incorporated the, &quot;Path of What I Wanted To Do Anyway&quot; and really Low Path Score people as a thing the Sabbat have to deal with. I have moments where the actual Path followers just EXPLODE on the Caine Bros with how embarrassing they're making the Sabbat and cause look.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/2j3adcbEwSM\" data-code=\"2j3adcbEwSM\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/2j3adcbEwSM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T00:45:49-07:00","id":1440419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440417#post1440417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the funny things is I actually incorporated the, &quot;Path of What I Wanted To Do Anyway&quot; and really Low Path Score people as a thing the Sabbat have to deal with. I have moments where the actual Path followers just EXPLODE on the Caine Bros with how embarrassing they're making the Sabbat and cause look.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is something often overlooked. What does a low Path score actually mean? A lot of Sabbat likely have low Path scores not because they're actually choosing to not follow it's tenets, but because they actually don't understand or comprehend the Path. These Sabbat think their Path, or perhaps even all Paths, are the &quot;Path of What I Wanted to Do Anyway&quot; and because they're not actually constraining the Beast in any way, the Beast is winning. The stranger the Path is to our eyes, the more likely its Sabbat adherents fail to truly understand it.<br /> <br /> It's like how in the Wraith setting, it is established that there is a significant number of Wraiths who can be overwhelmed by their Shadow at any time, and this presents a significant problem.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat should be dealing with that too. What do you do when you have a lot of vampires in your sect you can see degenerating, and you know it is only a matter of time before that becomes a threat to you? You either have to deal with it yourself by culling those vampires; or you call a &quot;Crusade&quot; and send off all of them to some Camarilla or Anarch city so they get killed off or tip off the witch hunters or lupines to do it for you.<br /> <br /> This should actually be a significant element to the sect.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I think this is probably the biggest reason Sabbat would choose to follow the Path of Evil Revelations because obeying a master who tells you what to do is fairly easy tenets to grasp. A lot of Sabbat with low Path scores who are close to losing themselves to the Beast are probably desperate to do anything to prevent the Beast from taking over. So an argument of &quot;Let me introduce you to my Master. He's really helped me regain control over the Beast. He can do the same for your&quot; should work very well to those kinds of vampires. Just like how actual cults recruit people in desperate need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T00:47:05-07:00","id":1440420,"title":"","content":"I just want to refuse to acknowledge that -Gehenna is now and it's lame- is a thing. Maybe it's a false Gehenna, maybe it's just a bunch of methuselah waking up and the new pope wants to establish his legitimacy with a crusade. Maybe they just want to kill of all the neonates in shipping containers and join the cam.. whatever, but it's not Gehenna. An apocalypse should be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T00:53:15-07:00","id":1440422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440420#post1440420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to refuse to acknowledge that -Gehenna is now and it's lame- is a thing. Maybe it's a false Gehenna, maybe it's just a bunch of methuselah waking up and the new pope wants to establish his legitimacy with a crusade. Maybe they just want to kill of all the neonates in shipping containers and join the cam.. whatever, but it's not Gehenna. An apocalypse should be fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may not be Gehenna but I always assumed the Antediluvians had a pattern:<br /> <br /> * Wake up<br /> * Summon your childer<br /> * Eat the unworthy<br /> * Bless the worthy<br /> * Make some grand epic proclamations<br /> * Go back to sleep<br /> * Repeat<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T01:15:00-07:00","id":1440426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godforsaken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440411#post1440411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For as long as I remember myself playing Vampire, we always did it very supernatural light, street level, personal problems type of game, when meeting another kindred was a really big deal for the PCs, and the world kinda felt lonely and unknown.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this was a very common style of game when Vampire was first introduced. But as more clans and bloodlines were introduced, the focus of the game switched from being a game of personal horror to a monster of the week or battles with your favorite enemy sect. When LARP became popular and people became used to large gatherings of vampires, the game moved even further because the center of a vampire's life now became a social life based around the Prince's court, or the Anarch hang out, or whatever.<br /> <br /> I like that earlier style too, but admit I struggle trying to find the right balance because there's a lot of cool toys in the other box as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T01:22:32-07:00","id":1440427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440422#post1440422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This may not be Gehenna but I always assumed the Antediluvians had a pattern:<br /> <br /> * Wake up<br /> * Summon your childer<br /> * Eat the unworthy<br /> * Bless the worthy<br /> * Make some grand epic proclamations<br /> * Go back to sleep<br /> * Repeat</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://memegenerator.net/img/instances/85338453/this-is-our-sixth-gehenna-and-weve-become-exceedingly-efficient-at-it.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T02:16:17-07:00","id":1440429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440413#post1440413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the funny things is that a lot of people think that the Sabbat are a group I don't like when they're easily my second favorite sect in the game. The Anarchs edge them out but only by a little.<br /> <br /> 1)I think the primary appeal of the Sabbat is the divorce from the human element of the game and the focus on the vampire element of the game, which doesn't mean that your characters are less likely to have friends, fall in love, be willing to die for one person, or have deep emotional torment. Essentially, it's just that your &quot;side&quot; is now your fellow vampires and all the people that you are invested in are among the Damned.<br /> <br /> I actually don't play the Sabbat as fundamentally that different from the Garou, which is an interesting parallel that I think fans of both might object to. The Sabbat KNOW that the world is under the control of the Antediluvians and the Camarilla is a disease that is going to rot them all out so you need to fight the latter to fight the former. However, that war is complicated by all manner of internal politics, weird spirituality, and infighting as well as people who only get the CAINITE MYTHOLOGY FOR DUMMIES version of your religion.<br /> <br /> 2)One of my favorite conversations in-game was about, of all things, love. The Sabbat leader said that if he did love any of the people in his mortal life then he should change them. If he doesn't then ask, &quot;Why are you willing to see them age, rot, and die? When you can instead love them for eternity.&quot;<br /> <br /> Said romantic elder also committed suicide because his partner for centuries died. It was all very tragic.<br /> <br /> 3)Another bit was where a Sabbat Elder basically said that he hated &quot;human head soccer&quot;, fleshcrafted furniture, and torturing mortals because it was so...silly. It was like humans going out and torturing animals. It was beneath the dignity of Sabbat. He gladly killed humans for a meal and didn't hesitate to kill to protect their secrets or for resources but the sadism against them was just a reflection of what he considered to be lingering Humanity. The Sabbat don't romanticize humans or Humanity--the worst elements of Kindred society are the same as mortals so why pretend they're better?<br /> <br /> Sabbat aren't just inhuman, they are POST-HUMAN and have their own morality, beliefs, culture, and religion that focuses on different things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Repeat after me for 1, 2 and 3 : depends on the Path <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> All that you say is valid, for followers of certain Paths (the Priests and Elders not caring about most games is probably always true mind)<br /> <br /> 2) I don't see many who made it to elder still caring about, or even remembering, who they were, but again ,some Paths lead that way, Harmony does (la la la la it still exists la la la ), in a strange way Path of Lilith maybe some others, Bones and Caine probably not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T02:19:40-07:00","id":1440430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440429#post1440429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Repeat after me for 1, 2 and 3 : depends on the Path <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> All that you say is valid, for followers of certain Paths (the Priests and Elders not caring about most games is probably always true mind)<br /> <br /> 2) I don't see many who made it to elder still caring about, or even remembering, who they were, but again ,some Paths lead that way, Harmony does (la la la la it still exists la la la ), in a strange way Path of Lilith maybe some others, Bones and Caine probably not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Elders in this case were suggesting that the Embrace is a way of beginning your new life. Humans are unimportant until they become vampires and even then that is the start of a long road of immortality.<br /> <br /> Before?<br /> <br /> Just the soil you play a seed in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T02:27:00-07:00","id":1440431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440430#post1440430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Elders in this case were suggesting that the Embrace is a way of beginning your new life. Humans are unimportant until they become vampires and even then that is the start of a long road of immortality.<br /> <br /> Before?<br /> <br /> Just the soil you play a seed in.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You mentioned a lovelorn suicide, which does seem more Humanity, than a lot of the Paths, (tho Chaining the Beast did short hand low path ratings with human disorders, which was probably unwise, but they did at least make it clear they were talking pop-psych not actually medical diagnostics). So, more humane, rather than Human elders in that case. But then I have made my positions clear on Paths pretty clear, and Touchstones more so. (If I am not making much sense, waiting for painkillers to kick in, so a bit distracted )<br /> <br /> Oh side idea, back with Infernalists.. how about a kind of Sub-Sect, an inverted Inconnu or Talmahera, worming through the other sects and the independents like a parasite? The Sabbat caught them at it (Hence inquisition) but is also more vulnerable (because already a series of Cults), but they infest every where they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 03-18-2021, 05:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T02:32:57-07:00","id":1440432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440431#post1440431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mentioned a lovelorn suicide, which does seem more Humanity, than a lot of the Paths, (tho Chaining the Beast did short hand low path ratings with human disorders, which was probably unwise, but they did at least make it clear they were talking pop-psych not actually medical diagnostics). So, more humane, rather than Human elders in that case. But then I have made my positions clear on Paths pretty clear, and Touchstones more so. (If I am not making much sense, waiting for painkillers to kick in, so a bit distracted )</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;Humans are incapable of love. It's a simple fact. They are incapable of knowing the deep abiding pure love that exists between pack mates and the Vaulderie as well as centuries of time. Only vampires, as the children of Caine, have the passion and spiritual superiority to be able to truly know someone as well as bond with them.<br /> <br /> Some Elders or Paths disdain love but others would note that the bonds the Sabbat have between members be they marriage, Pack Bonds, and rituals are far deeper than any Kine could understand. Like the epic warriors of old, when Achilles lost his cousin Paltroclus, they feel the agony and pain of such a bond being severed. Brothers in blood far thicker than those of mere genetic stock but battle, fang, and ritual. Because they are alive and humans are not.<br /> <br /> Vampires may be dead but Kine never truly live.&quot;</i><br /> -My Serpent of Light character<br /> <br /> But I like to play the Sabbat as epic operatic warriors with greater passion than mere mortals.<br /> <br /> Like <i>300 </i>without the racism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-18-2021, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T02:37:12-07:00","id":1440433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440432#post1440432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Humans are incapable of love. It's a simple fact. They are incapable of knowing the deep abiding pure love that exists between pack mates and the Vaulderie as well as centuries of time. Only vampires, as the children of Caine, have the passion and spiritual superiority to be able to truly know someone as well as bond with them.<br /> <br /> *puts in Hesha monocle*<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You had one referencing mortal love tho (unless I misunderstood something).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T02:39:04-07:00","id":1440434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440433#post1440433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You had one referencing mortal love tho (unless I misunderstood something).</div> </div> </div> </div>I had one say that if a person loved a mortal, they should Embrace them because it's a parody of love to leave someone as a weak fragile human.<br /> <br /> Basically saying a proper Sabbat does not romanticize humanity. It is an ugly horrible condition to them and they lack the Camarilla (more the Toreador's) weird fascination with it. I also said that they love other vampires because humans are simply animals to them and possibly not even that. Humans are background noise to the Sabbat as a general rule.<br /> <br /> I don't think Sabbat could have human Touchstones because the very premise is impossible. Sabbat do not RESPECT humans so they can't draw from them any moral centering.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Camarilla Player Character: Oh, Bob is such a good husband and loving father. He reminds me of the days I had a living family and I feel like if I study Bob, I can remember what it is like to be human.<br /> <br /> Sabbat Player Character: Bob is a fat office clerk who watches porn every night to get it up for his wife. He's also going to be dead in a couple of decades, just like his family so who gives a shit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-18-2021, 05:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T02:46:46-07:00","id":1440436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440434#post1440434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had one say that if a person loved a mortal, they should Embrace them because it's a parody of love to leave someone as a weak fragile human.<br /> <br /> Basically saying a proper Sabbat does not romanticize humanity. It is an ugly horrible condition to them and they lack the Camarilla (more the Toreador's) weird fascination with it. I also said that they love other vampires because humans are simply animals to them and possibly not even that. Humans are background noise to the Sabbat as a general rule.<br /> <br /> I don't think Sabbat could have human Touchstones because the very premise is impossible. Sabbat do not RESPECT humans so they can't draw from them any moral centering.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Camarilla Player Character: Oh, Bob is such a good husband and loving father. He reminds me of the days I had a living family and I feel like if I study Bob, I can remember what it is like to be human.<br /> <br /> Sabbat Player Character: Bob is a fat office clerk who watches porn every night to get it up for his wife. He's also going to be dead in a couple of decades, just like his family so who gives a shit?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't think anyone can draw moral centering from other people. Like at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T02:49:21-07:00","id":1440437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440436#post1440436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone can draw moral centering from other people. Like at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's one of the most basic ways people do it.<br /> <br /> &quot;What would Jesus do?&quot;<br /> <br /> Or otherwise looking to other people for guidance on how to behave. It's just exaggerated for vampires because if you're not aging and the world is moving around you, you need someone to imitate and understand to give you a sense of how people should behave.<br /> <br /> Vampires aren't human so a vampire on Humanity needing humans to remind them of how to be human seems reasonable.<br /> <br /> Vampires on Paths? No. That's silly.<br /> <br /> Humans are pack creatures, though, so having someone reinforce your morality and sense of reality helps. TRUE BLOOD actually did it with vampires that lived in &quot;Nests&quot; all becoming homicidal psychopaths after awhile. Well, more so than vampires who regularly associated with humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T03:09:51-07:00","id":1440439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440413#post1440413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually don't play the Sabbat as fundamentally that different from the Garou, which is an interesting parallel that I think fans of both might object to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the comparison with the Garou is a pretty good one. It should be easy for everyone to grok the differences between default <i>Vampire</i> chronicles and default <i>Werewolf</i> chronicles. You can certainly do personal horror and fear of losing loved ones in <i>Werewolf,</i> too, but sometimes you just gotta tear a fool's face off in righteous rage. The Sabbat lean more into the latter style of play than the former. It's no wonder that the developer who wrote the original Sabbat books, Steven C. Brown, was also interested in <i>Vampire-Werewolf</i> crossovers -- he's also the author of <i>Under a Blood Red Moon,</i> after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T03:12:12-07:00","id":1440440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440437#post1440437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's one of the most basic ways people do it.<br /> <br /> &quot;What would Jesus do?&quot;<br /> <br /> Or otherwise looking to other people for guidance on how to behave. It's just exaggerated for vampires because if you're not aging and the world is moving around you, you need someone to imitate and understand to give you a sense of how people should behave.<br /> <br /> Vampires aren't human so a vampire on Humanity needing humans to remind them of how to be human seems reasonable.<br /> <br /> Vampires on Paths? No. That's silly.<br /> <br /> Humans are pack creatures, though, so having someone reinforce your morality and sense of reality helps. TRUE BLOOD actually did it with vampires that lived in &quot;Nests&quot; all becoming homicidal psychopaths after awhile. Well, more so than vampires who regularly associated with humans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> WWJD isn't focusing in on one person as the only thing letting you hold onto part of your sanity tho. Like, I can think Nelson Mandela was a good but flawed man who achieved great things (which is all you can really expect from a human, we are all flawed, it's kinda our thing), without him being the only thing stopping me doing something.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T03:58:36-07:00","id":1440441,"title":"","content":"From the experience of basically everybody who isn't into the bible, people tend to use the bible to justify whatever they want. WWJD is like telling your kids/friends to behave because they're embarrasing you/will probably drag you down with whatever bullshit they're doing that Jesus wouldn't. But they rarely actually live to the standards of jesus when it's inconvenient for them. The people that do live up to Jesus's-standards were probably nice guys anyway, or at least susceptible to peer pressure, and would likely still be nice without jesus. Of course, you might be influenced by Jesus, but to actually be like Jesus you've still gotta be on the same kind of wavelength. <br /> <br /> So, yeah, stalking bob doesn't make you more moral. Your problems are your own and you're mentally unfit if you are absolutely dependent upon some externalization you've put onto someone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T06:21:00-07:00","id":1440452,"title":"","content":"to me the human touchstone limitation seems to exist because the most logical way to translate paths to touchstones is by limiting what touchstones you can take and anything more complicated then &quot;humanity can only have human touchstones&quot; would be to confusing for the wider audience that they're aiming for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T10:25:34-07:00","id":1440464,"title":"","content":"The two big emotional problems vampires face is the urge to eat to gluttony whenever even slightly hungry, and the urge to destroy when even slightly angry. All Paths, and I'm counting Humanity as a Path in this context, are attempts to fight this with intense belief.<br /> <br /> Humanity - I will not eat to gluttony or rage at the slightest provocation because that would be evil.<br /> <br /> Feral Heart - I will not eat to gluttony or rage at the slightest provocation because that is self-destructive and therefore beneath the cunning, forward-seeing, perfect predator I aspire to be.<br /> <br /> Honorable Accord - I will not eat to gluttony or rage at the slightest provocation because that would violate my oaths, either directly or by rendering direct upholding of those oaths impossible.(In other words I can't protect the Sabbat if I am dead, running from the police, or have attracted hunters to the Sabbat with my foolishness. And I certainly can't uphold, say, my oath to protect the Archbishop if I attack him because he was slightly rude to me.)<br /> <br /> That's why I've never understood the Path of Cathari, because it really doesn't seem to have a belief system that would prevent you from eating to gluttony at the slightest hunger or raging at the slightest provocation. Even the Path of Evil Revelations has better motive for that: I will not eat to gluttony or rage at the slightest provocation because that would be counterproductive to the interests of my master.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T11:10:53-07:00","id":1440471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440441#post1440441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the experience of basically everybody who isn't into the bible, people tend to use the bible to justify whatever they want. WWJD is like telling your kids/friends to behave because they're embarrasing you/will probably drag you down with whatever bullshit they're doing that Jesus wouldn't. But they rarely actually live to the standards of jesus when it's inconvenient for them. The people that do live up to Jesus's-standards were probably nice guys anyway, or at least susceptible to peer pressure, and would likely still be nice without jesus. Of course, you might be influenced by Jesus, but to actually be like Jesus you've still gotta be on the same kind of wavelength.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, stalking bob doesn't make you more moral. Your problems are your own and you're mentally unfit if you are absolutely dependent upon some externalization you've put onto someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>You think you're actually arguing against Touchstones when you're actually arguing for them. All of this just seems like stuff that would be part of the issue of being in a vampire's life.<br /> <br /> The &quot;fun&quot; is the fact that making a person your Morality Chain is a terible way to do it even if it works....for the vampire....in keeping them somewhat sane.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I don't believe naturally &quot;nice&quot; or &quot;bad&quot; people exist as that's silly. You are responsible for your own actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440440#post1440440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WWJD isn't focusing in on one person as the only thing letting you hold onto part of your sanity tho. Like, I can think Nelson Mandela was a good but flawed man who achieved great things (which is all you can really expect from a human, we are all flawed, it's kinda our thing), without him being the only thing stopping me doing something.....</div> </div> </div> </div>You, as a human being, aren't likely to forget what its like to do as social norms, though. What's acceptable when talking to people. What is good and what is evil.<br /> <br /> Sabbat don't care because they make their own morality.<br /> <br /> Camarilla are all hypocrites and justify every action they do.<br /> <br /> Anarchs? Well, they do have human friends and associates.<br /> <br /> A Touchstone is just basically there to give a vampire a kind of reminder of human life to someone who is NOT human. &quot;Ah yes, my ghoul needs sleep and to use the bathroom. Should probably remember to let my employees have time for that when they do their jobs at Amazon.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440464#post1440464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I've never understood the Path of Cathari, because it really doesn't seem to have a belief system that would prevent you from eating to gluttony at the slightest hunger or raging at the slightest provocation. Even the Path of Evil Revelations has better motive for that: I will not eat to gluttony or rage at the slightest provocation because that would be counterproductive to the interests of my master.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Path of Cathari was just, &quot;Get high, have sex, eat your fill nightly, and the Beast won't bother you because it's satisfied.&quot; Which is something I'd assume has a higher spiritual element but most wouldn't see.<br /> <br /> Then again, I see it as the descendant of THE ROAD OF THE DEVIL that split into it and the Path of Evil Revelations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-18-2021, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T12:38:57-07:00","id":1440486,"title":"","content":"Picking up from another thread...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440302-la-by-night-full-update?p=1440472#post1440472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat seems to be the least free of any sect since, well, it's an army. It can really provide many benefits but freedom seems like the thing they can give least vs. the Anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would chalk that up to edition differences, again. Even the characterization of the Sabbat as an army (the so-called Sword of Caine) is a Revised invention. The 2nd Edition presentation of the sect is a melting pot of various fringe beliefs rather than an army. All Sabbat vampires are dedicated to the destruction of the Antediluvians, but different factions of the Sabbat pursue that goal in different ways across the globe. Consider the following: &quot;Sabbat vampires differ from other vampires in their overwhelming loyalty to their sect and their belief in personal freedom. <b>The Sabbat is founded on these two principles: loyalty and freedom. All their activities promote them.</b>&quot; (<i>The Players Guide to the Sabbat,</i> page 30, &quot;Sabbat Ideology&quot;; emphasis mine.)<br /> <br /> If you take those words seriously -- <i>all Sabbat activities promote loyalty and freedom</i> -- there's little room for an interpretation where the Sabbat are, in fact, the least free of all the sects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T12:42:25-07:00","id":1440489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440486#post1440486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Picking up from another thread...I would chalk that up to edition differences, again. Even the characterization of the Sabbat as an army (the so-called Sword of Caine) is a Revised invention. The 2nd Edition presentation of the sect is a melting pot of various fringe beliefs rather than an army. All Sabbat vampires are dedicated to the destruction of the Antediluvians, but different factions of the Sabbat pursue that goal in different ways across the globe. Consider the following: &quot;Sabbat vampires differ from other vampires in their overwhelming loyalty to their sect and their belief in personal freedom. <b>The Sabbat is founded on these two principles: loyalty and freedom. All their activities promote them.</b>&quot; (<i>The Players Guide to the Sabbat,</i> page 30, &quot;Sabbat Ideology&quot;; emphasis mine.)<br /> <br /> If you take those words seriously -- <i>all Sabbat activities promote loyalty and freedom</i> -- there's little room for an interpretation where the Sabbat are, in fact, the least free of all the sects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its not a retcon necessarily to question whether the Sabbat's belief about that are accurate given that they are all Blood Bound to one another, do nightly rituals to bind each other together, kidnap people off the street to indoctrinate them into the Sword of Caine's religon, and are sworn to the military. Plus they answer to a much more organized heirarchy than the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> This is all 2nd Edition too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T13:31:16-07:00","id":1440492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440489#post1440489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think its not a retcon necessarily to question whether the Sabbat's belief about that are accurate given that they are all Blood Bound to one another, do nightly rituals to bind each other together, kidnap people off the street to indoctrinate them into the Sword of Caine's religon, and are sworn to the military. Plus they answer to a much more organized heirarchy than the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat is an insane millenarianist cult, yes. But they are also the only vampires in the world who are free from the Blood Bond. Comparing the Vinculum to being Blood Bound to one another does not sit right with me; the Vaulderie would never have caught on if they were in any way comparable. The Vinculum is a much lower level effect, especially since most Sabbat are not going to have anywhere near maximum Vinculum ratings with one another.<br /> <br /> This is why I don't like the anarchs as their separate sect: they have no answers to the fundamental aspects of vampiric existence. What stops anarch leaders from employing the Blood Bond exactly like the Camarilla? Moral fiber? If true egality is so easy among the undead as it apparently is among the Anarch Movement, all other sects are left without any leg to stand on. The setting needs to show areas of unlife where the anarchs behave <i>much worse</i> than either the Camarilla or the Sabbat if they're going to be an interesting sect of their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T14:59:55-07:00","id":1440500,"title":"","content":"I agree a lot with Elphilim's take. One of the biggest problems I had with the Revised depiction of the Sabbat is that it basically ignored the Loyalists (and sympathetic moderates and opportunistic groups like the Panders who could go any way depending on what was at stake) so it could put &quot;the Sword of Caine&quot; onto the metaplot railroad that required lots of Crusades.<br /> <br /> There are certainly Sabbat that fit the &quot;Sword of Caine&quot; motif of Revised. They're called the Black Hand. There are a lot of ambitious and tyrannical elders who want the entire sect to be so centralized and obedient to them - primarily the elder Lasombra and Tzimisce of the episcopate along with some others. That's why there were the Sabbat Civil Wars. The sect is increasingly becoming more authoritarian, but the centralizers have not yet triumphed and they have a lot of opponents.<br /> <br /> But there are lots of other styles and groups of Sabbat out there. I imagine there are some Loyalist nomad packs or even covens that are practically indistinguishable from the Anarchs or even Camarilla loyal wandering Gangrel.<br /> <br /> I think it's an important issue of the Vaulderie and how often it is performed and with who. Some packs will perform it very rarely and only amidst themselves. I imagine many Loyalist nomad packs do this approach - they are very concerned about the freedom of its members. Then there will be packs that perform it more frequently, but still less so with others. And there's an entire spectrum where at the end are Sabbat that perform the Vaulderie all the time and with as many Sabbat as they can. I think many of the centralizers of the Sabbat encourage frequent and promiscuous Vaulderie as a way they can control other Sabbat, so a major issue of the Loyalists should be regulating these kind of calls.<br /> <br /> The organized militant hierarchy CTPhipps mentioned is one example of the Sabbat, but it is not the only. It needs a good mix of styles in order to show the diversity within the Sabbat, and how the sect's internal conflicts and contradicting impulses relate and interact.<br /> <br /> I think the game would benefit by having more By Night books that present different styles of Sabbat. Montreal was fine for for a stable, but hierarchical Sabbat really interested in outre occultism and spiritualism (though I find it a little too gonzo and should be toned down). But we need an example of a domain with a more practical tyrannical Sabbat approach of elders wanting to keep tight central control. And a place where Loyalist Sabbat dominant and show the sect in an aspect the idealistic remnants of the Anarch Revolt would like. These would all be very different styles of Sabbat, but all very much Sabbat.<br /> <br /> But I prefer a Sabbat that is highly divided and struggles with the antagonisms different factions produce with each other. I think it offers more opportunity for roleplay, but within a Sabbat only game and as an element in non-Sabbat games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 03-18-2021, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T15:34:42-07:00","id":1440503,"title":"","content":"I think it was always the biggest mistake of the writing of the Anarchs to make them considered to be part of the Camarilla because I always felt that it nerfed them to the point that the Sabbat ate a huge chunk of what I consider to be the Movement's appeal. If you are actually against the Camarilla's feudal system of government, if you think the Camarilla is a bunch of tyrants and portray their leadership as bad guys, then it seems like the Anarchs just sit around doing absolutely nothing.<br /> <br /> Part of this is the set up. With the exception of the Anarch Free States (established through violent revolution), there are no Anarch Free States. The Brujah Council was destroyed prior to 1st Edition in the backstory. The Camarilla doesn't negotiate with Anarchs. Not since the Treaty of Thorns, which could charitably be called the Anarchs surrendering after being beaten by the Elders. Which is not again anything for someone who wants to play defiant rebels.<br /> <br /> Basically, the portrayal of the Anarchs form Second Edition to Revised emphasized them as the Camarilla's prison bitches. The Anarchs were even fighting tooth and claw by the side of the Camarilla's flunkies against the Sabbat. They're also doing this seemingly for no reward or benefit despite the fact that they're on the frontlines in 1999. This actually gets shown in 1999's WINTER'S TEETH where the Anarchs discuss fighting the Sabbat and how the Camarilla immediately turned on them afterward (which I feel is very appropriate and believable for the Ivory Tower).<br /> <br /> I feel like having the Anarchs successfully overthrow multiple cities and take a hardline stance against the Camarilla actually makes them more dramatically interesting even in places where the Camarilla and Anarchs are being peaceful. In Chicago, say, you have Kevin Jackson tolerate Anita Wainwright and the other Anarchs because he CAN'T kill them and has to negotiate with them because war is a bad thing.<br /> <br /> Not because he wouldn't kill them if he could.<br /> <br /> That's my take at least.<br /> <br /> Because a simmering Cold War that can break out into a hot war is better than a &quot;peace&quot; that has the Anarchs utterly powerless before the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T16:50:07-07:00","id":1440507,"title":"","content":"My problem with the current setup is that even though the anarchs are not necessarily the good guys, they are infinitely more reasonable than any of the alternatives, and the no-brainer choice for every character who isn't a total shitbird. When they were presented as part of the Camarilla, I honestly found them a lot more sympathetic, because at least back then the anarchs <i>had</i> one major flaw: they were too decentralized and disorganized to ever affect any real change, at least on a scale larger than the example provided in the Anarch Free State.<br /> <br /> Now that the anarchs are apparently organized, effective, and poised to make Anarch Free States the default model of society for all Kindred, what role can the other sects have but be pure antagonists? Why would any sensible person who just wants to unlive and let unlive <i>ever</i> choose the Camarilla over the Anarchs? What could the Sabbat possibly offer to anyone but total psychopaths when the anarchs make real equality, modern systems of government, the democratic process, and freedom from Blood Bonds look easy? I think this is what people mean when they say that the game treats the anarchs with kid gloves: they don't <i>have</i> a major flaw like the other sects do.<br /> <br /> If there is no sensible reason why a character would choose another sect over the Anarch Movement, I feel like the sect has failed as a concept. One of the reasons why I like the old World of Darkness is that a newly made vampire only has crap options to choose from. Like every person in the real world, vampires find themselves subject to vast structures of law and tradition invented hundreds of years before they were born. It's up to the players to make something of the shit sandwich they are dealt at the start. I don't need a faction that is obviously morally superior to every other option and effective at pursuing its goals and objectives as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T17:02:04-07:00","id":1440508,"title":"","content":"I think the major problem with the Anarchs after 1994 was the lack of specific examples of what they intended to do. Simply being against &quot;the Man&quot; only goes so far. We needed some specific groups and their aims. If all they are is &quot;replace the Prince with a better Prince&quot;, there's only so much mileage you can get out of it. A lot of us expected Los Angeles By Night to be that sourcebook where we'd see these ideas in print. It wasn't. Even first edition Chicago By Night gave us different factions in the form of Maldavis, Hind's Socialists, and Juggler's Nihilists. It was still unclear what exactly they intended to replace Lodin with (or more ambitiously, the entire structure of the Inner Circle, Justicars, Conclaves, etc.), but at least we understood each stood for something different. The Barons of the LA Free States were just thugs as petty Princes with not much differentiating them except for personalities. We've discussed this on several threads now.<br /> <br /> I also agree that the depiction in Revised was not the best. It makes complete sense for the Anarchs and Camarilla to tactically team up against their mutual enemy, the Sabbat. But after surviving the initial attack, the Anarchs shouldn't have just shown up to help like elves (or Rohirrim cavlary charge if you prefer) at the siege of Helm's Deep. Anarch representatives would have cut a deal. &quot;We'll help you take New York, but in exchange we keep Brooklyn as a Free State.&quot; or &quot;Of course we'll help you take back Buffalo and Atlanta. We'll do that by attacking Baltimore ourselves. That'll free up enough of your forces to take those other two cities, and we'll defeat the Sabbat all together in three of them. That's what this is about, right? Of course, we expect the Justicar to acknowledge our domain at the next Conclave. Which needs to be held right now with all of us here. Just to make it official and on the record.&quot; The Camarilla will still try to wiggle out of their commitments afterwards, but at least the Anarchs won't seem stupid.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs have their elders and ancillae too, just like the Camarilla have their neonates. Anarch elders aren't going to be foot soldiers. They lead their own foot soldiers.<br /> <br /> But the Anarchs as a sect weren't important to the metaplot railroad in Revised so they got the shaft just like so many other concepts did. Lots of things were simply ignored because they were inconvenient for the plot. It's why I quickly sorrowed at Revised and stopped buying sourcebooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T17:03:27-07:00","id":1440509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440507#post1440507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with the current setup is that even though the anarchs are not necessarily the good guys, they are infinitely more reasonable than any of the alternatives, and the no-brainer choice for every character who isn't a total shitbird.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's Gothic PUNK.<br /> <br /> The whole point is being a rebel against the Man. The Anarchs are the Edgerunner faction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now that the anarchs are apparently organized, effective, and poised to make Anarch Free States the default model of society for all Kindred, what role can the other sects have but be pure antagonists? Why would any sensible person who just wants to unlive and let unlive <i>ever</i> choose the Camarilla over the Anarchs? </div> </div> </div>The Anarchs being organized and effective doesn't mean that they're better. They're still vampires and there's plenty of hypocrites among them. Remember, the first Anarch we meet is Juggler. Also, just because they're the moral faction doesn't mean they're the one people want to play. Not everyone wants to be the good guy, especially in a game where you are a traditional fantasy monster.<br /> <br /> Plenty of people want to play Camarilla to be rich, powerful, and terrifying.<br /> <br /> I play the Sabbat to be an erudite educated evil monster or a crazy lunatic in a Halloween-themed version of GTA.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If there is no sensible reason why a character would choose another sect over the Anarch Movement, I feel like the sect has failed as a concept. </div> </div> </div>Reasons: Money, Power, Snobbery, Clan","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-18-2021, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T17:05:54-07:00","id":1440510,"title":"","content":"I think part of the problem that Anarchs have defining themselves, is that feudalism is pretty much the default government of human beings, (and in this context vampires are mentally human) and can only be evolved past with immense efforts. Feudalism is what happens when alphas dominate small groups, and those alphas bow to bigger alphas, until there is a chain of alphas leading to what is, really, a king whether you use that word or not. Absolute freedom turns into feudalism just as fast as the alphas can establish a pecking order.Until then it's a bunch of warlords murdering other warlords.<br /> <br /> Moreover, the factors that allow humans to eventually evolve past feudalism don't apply to vampires. The people at the top aren't physically inferior to workers, don't die of old and leave the kingdom to their much softer children, and the people at the top don't really need the workers to, well, work. In fact, all the vampires are basically competition for all other vampires for feeding rights. It would be in the best interests of every vampire if every other vampire died, and the only thing really preventing that from gradually happening is vampires creating more competition because it aids in some short term goal, from loneliness to territorial defense.<br /> <br /> Because vampires inherently can't really get past feudalism, what's an anarch to really do? He can't change the system, he can only change who is on top. At which point he or she might just as well call themselves Camarilla and be done with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T17:11:35-07:00","id":1440512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440510#post1440510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because vampires inherently can't really get past feudalism, what's an anarch to really do? He can't change the system, he can only change who is on top. At which point he or she might just as well call themselves Camarilla and be done with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I described the Anarchs alternative to the Camarilla in my recent game as such:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">&quot;In a Camarilla city, the Prince and the Primogen and the Elders enforce their power through the violence of the powerful on the weak. Everything flows up. In a Anarch city, the Baron can be ripped apart by the vampires underneath him if he doesn't do a good job or kill only the guys who have it coming. The benefits flow down. This sounds not that different but is really fucking different. And yes, I note that I am the Baron.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T17:19:04-07:00","id":1440514,"title":"","content":"In the original write up of the first edition, the Camarilla is basically the &quot;state&quot;. In that regards, Anarchs had little choice but to somehow coexist with the Camarilla in the same way everyone have to live by the rule of law.<br /> <br /> In that sense, Anarchs played a role akin to shadowrunners. They were at the same time part of the system and out of it. Rebels without the means for meaningful change. Loyal to the Gothic Punk genre. (as a note even shadowrun has its Anarchist states &quot;free&quot; of corporations like East Berlin)<br /> Things mostly remained the same up to V20 with the Anarchs staying a counter-culture to both the Camarilla and the Sabbat forms of government.<br /> <br /> In V5 tough, Anarchs became a real faction. And thus they became the new establishment. Losing on the way a lot of their Punk flavor (and arguably Gothic too) to the detriment of everyone in the setting (Sabbat first regrettably).<br /> <br /> It's like if in Shadowrun, Anarcho-socialist states were a real alternative to the Corporatist mainstream instead of the rare gems of what could be. The setting suddenly loses a lot of the its Gothic Punk. And we are back to Red vs Blue cold war style of faction conflict where one is clearly morally superior to the other. (and ironically playing the worse faction become the &quot;edgy&quot; choice)<br /> <br /> It's... meh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 03-18-2021, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T17:27:07-07:00","id":1440516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440514#post1440514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the original write up of the first edition, the Camarilla is basically the &quot;state&quot;. In that regards, Anarchs had little choice but to somehow coexist with the Camarilla in the same way everyone have to live by the rule of law.<br /> <br /> In that sense, Anarchs played a role akin to shadowrunners. They were at the same time part of the system and out of it. Rebels without the means for meaningful change. Loyal to the Gothic Punk genre. (as a note even shadowrun has its Anarchist states &quot;free&quot; of corporations like East Berlin)<br /> Things mostly remained the same up to V20 with the Anarchs staying a counter-culture to both the Camarilla and the Sabbat forms of government.<br /> <br /> In V5 tough, Anarchs became a real faction. And thus they became the new establishment. Losing on the way a lot of their Punk flavor (and arguably Gothic too) to the detriment of everyone in the setting (Sabbat first regrettably).<br /> <br /> It's like if in Shadowrun, Anarcho-socialist states were a real alternative to the Corporatist mainstream instead of the rare gems of what could be. The setting suddenly loses a lot of the its Gothic Punk. And we are back to Red vs Blue cold war style of faction conflict where one is clearly morally superior to the other. (and ironically playing the worse faction become the &quot;edgy&quot; choice)<br /> <br /> It's... meh.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would actually argue quite wrong. I think you're CLOSE but missing the very real alternative that makes the V:TM world of 5th Edition work as a proper cyberpunk-esque setting.<br /> <br /> THE CAMARILLA: They are the Corpos. Easy comparison.<br /> <br /> THE ANARCHS: Are *NOT* Edgerunners. The Anarchs are the CRIMINALS. The Yakuza, the Mafia, the gangs, and so on.<br /> <br /> THE PCS: Are the Edgerunners.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs aren't good guys but they're arguably the lesser evil and can still screw you. Judge like Dex in Cyberpunk 2077.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T17:27:43-07:00","id":1440517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440509#post1440509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it's Gothic PUNK.<br /> <br /> The whole point is being a rebel against the Man.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, to hear Mark Rein-Hagen talk about how he came up with the clans and what he imagined the game would be about, rebelling against The Man isn't exactly it: &quot;I always thought of the clans in terms of a primogen council meeting. You know, seven people around the table -- how are they interacting? Each clan, I always imagined them at a council table, and how are they talking to each other. [...] So the Toreador has the tart, kind of acidic humor, biting; the Tremere is the imperious outsider; the Ventrue is desperately trying to hold everyone together and get their agenda through; and so on.&quot; (Timestamped video <b><a href=\"https://youtu.be/Of1JmwBlmNc?t=2526\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></b> for anyone who's interested.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plenty of people want to play Camarilla to be rich, powerful, and terrifying.<br /> <br /> I play the Sabbat to be an erudite educated evil monster or a crazy lunatic in a Halloween-themed version of GTA. </div> </div> </div>That's kind of my point -- only total pieces of shit would ever choose the Camarilla or the Sabbat now. Are there any sensible reasons to throw in with either sect? There used to be, when the anarchs were easy to see as too ineffective in achieving their stated goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T17:32:15-07:00","id":1440518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440508#post1440508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the major problem with the Anarchs after 1994 was the lack of specific examples of what they intended to do. Simply being against &quot;the Man&quot; only goes so far. We needed some specific groups and their aims. If all they are is &quot;replace the Prince with a better Prince&quot;, there's only so much mileage you can get out of it. A lot of us expected Los Angeles By Night to be that sourcebook where we'd see these ideas in print. It wasn't. Even first edition Chicago By Night gave us different factions in the form of Maldavis, Hind's Socialists, and Juggler's Nihilists. It was still unclear what exactly they intended to replace Lodin with (or more ambitiously, the entire structure of the Inner Circle, Justicars, Conclaves, etc.), but at least we understood each stood for something different. The Barons of the LA Free States were just thugs as petty Princes with not much differentiating them except for personalities. We've discussed this on several threads now.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my WIR of LA by Night I felt that the book was designed around two concepts that led to a lot of of unfortunate implications. LA By Night was designed around a V:TM setting that would be very good for combat-heavy &quot;action&quot; games by having it be in a constant state of gang warfare. It's pretty much a place for Sabbat-esque games without the war on the Camarilla. The tastelessness of using the real life gang violence of LA during the 90s as a basis for &quot;fun&quot; gang warfare and not acknowledging the many young men (and others) killed being one of the more unfortunate things in the book.<br /> <br /> The second concept was that it was an attempt to make a &quot;deep&quot; claim about the Anarchs not really being any different than the Camarilla. Both sides are the SAME Edgelordness was very popular in the 90s and there's always been some of that (Juggler and Modius are identical) but it kind of left the Anarchs in a bad place.<br /> <br /> &quot;Say what you will about the Sabbat but at least they are an ethos.&quot; - The Big Lebowski by Night<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also agree that the depiction in Revised was not the best. It makes complete sense for the Anarchs and Camarilla to tactically team up against their mutual enemy, the Sabbat. But after surviving the initial attack, the Anarchs shouldn't have just shown up to help like elves (or Rohirrim cavlary charge if you prefer) at the siege of Helm's Deep. Anarch representatives would have cut a deal. &quot;We'll help you take New York, but in exchange we keep Brooklyn as a Free State.&quot; or &quot;Of course we'll help you take back Buffalo and Atlanta. We'll do that by attacking Baltimore ourselves. That'll free up enough of your forces to take those other two cities, and we'll defeat the Sabbat all together in three of them. That's what this is about, right? Of course, we expect the Justicar to acknowledge our domain at the next Conclave. Which needs to be held right now with all of us here. Just to make it official and on the record.&quot; The Camarilla will still try to wiggle out of their commitments afterwards, but at least the Anarchs won't seem stupid. </div> </div> </div>I agree with this and actually would love for this to have been part of why the Brujah and Gangrel's defection. The idea that a lot of promises were made during the Sabbat Crusade by Jan Pieterszoon and other East Coast Camarilla leaders only to be immediately betrayed once the war was over.<br /> <br /> Like Lawrence of Arabia: &quot;If we've told lies, you've told half-lies. And the man who tells lies, like me, merely hides the truth. But the man who tells half-lies has forgotten where he's put it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the Anarchs as a sect weren't important to the metaplot railroad in Revised so they got the shaft just like so many other concepts did. Lots of things were simply ignored because they were inconvenient for the plot. It's why I quickly sorrowed at Revised and stopped buying sourcebooks. </div> </div> </div>I am of the opinion they actually had planned to write the Anarchs out of the game entirely. The Sabbat was going to take its position as the opposition sect while the Camarilla would absorb the remaining Anarchs. They were also going to replace the Anarchs with the Kuei-Jin as they had the latter wipe out the Anarch Free States completely.<br /> <br /> However, then Bloodlines reminded people why they liked Anarchs and the Kuei-Jin proved to be FAR less popular than expected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T17:32:39-07:00","id":1440519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440516#post1440516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would actually argue quite wrong. I think you're CLOSE but missing the very real alternative that makes the V:TM world of 5th Edition work as a proper cyberpunk-esque setting.<br /> <br /> THE CAMARILLA: They are the Corpos. Easy comparison.<br /> <br /> THE ANARCHS: Are *NOT* Edgerunners. The Anarchs are the CRIMINALS. The Yakuza, the Mafia, the gangs, and so on.<br /> <br /> THE PCS: Are the Edgerunners.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs aren't good guys but they're arguably the lesser evil and can still screw you. Judge like Dex in Cyberpunk 2077.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would work if the Camarilla and Anarch were not antagonistic but different &quot;businesses&quot; that either work or fight each other with no ideological string attached. (Like some Requiem factions -not all of them tough-)<br /> <br /> Obviously, this is not the case. The Anarch paint themselves as an alternative to the Camarilla rule, it's the whole reason of their existence. To struggle against the Camarilla. So if the Camarilla are the Corpos, then the Anarch are the Anarchist of Shadowun.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really matter that the Anarch are not the good guys or not. As long as they are far better than the Camarilla or the Sabbat, they undermine the setting just as much as Anarchism would in Shadowrun. Because they are no more Rebels. Only sides now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 03-18-2021, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T17:34:07-07:00","id":1440520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440519#post1440519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would work if the Camarilla and Anarch were not antagonistic but different &quot;businesses&quot; that either work or fight each other with no ideological string attached.<br /> <br /> Obviously, this is not the case. The Anarch paint themselves as an alternative to the Camarilla rule. So if the Camarilla are the Corpos, the Anarch are the Anarchist of Shadowun.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really matter that the Anarch are not the good guys or not. As long as they are far better than the Camarilla or the Sabbat, they undermine the setting just as much as Anarchism would in Shadowrun.</div> </div> </div> </div>What we've seen in Chicago by Night is that the Anarchs live in the same cities the Camarilla and vice versa. They just live in different territory and tolerate each other while feuding.<br /> <br /> Like...gangs.<br /> <br /> Mafia as well as street.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T17:35:38-07:00","id":1440521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440512#post1440512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I described the Anarchs alternative to the Camarilla in my recent game as such:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">&quot;In a Camarilla city, the Prince and the Primogen and the Elders enforce their power through the violence of the powerful on the weak. Everything flows up. In a Anarch city, the Baron can be ripped apart by the vampires underneath him if he doesn't do a good job or kill only the guys who have it coming. The benefits flow down. This sounds not that different but is really fucking different. And yes, I note that I am the Baron.&quot;</span></div> </div> </div> </div>That just sounds like what you get when there is a weak prince and a powerful primogen council. It also sounds a lot like how Rome was during the period when the Emperor was a figurehead, and Rome was really ruled by a military junta. During that period, any time the Emperor would annoy the military junta, the junta would just kill him and put out a bunch of propaganda that he was a complete nutter who needed killing. It's not remembered as a wonderful time of great freedom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T17:36:50-07:00","id":1440522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440521#post1440521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That just sounds like what you get when there is a weak prince and a powerful primogen council. It also sounds a lot like how Rome was during the period when the Emperor was a figurehead, and Rome was really ruled by a military junta. During that period, any time the Emperor would annoy the military junta, the junta would just kill him and put out a bunch of propaganda that he was a complete nutter who needed killing. It's not remembered as a wonderful time of great freedom.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference between a Primogen and every vampire in a city is the size of the vampires present in a vampire domain. It should be noted the largest vampire community in the world is probably around 200.<br /> <br /> Vampire Democracy is kind of ridiculous when the number of New York or Paris' Kindred is the size of a single American classroom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T17:48:45-07:00","id":1440523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440520#post1440520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like...gangs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or... states.<br /> <br /> That they coexist is the actual issue here. You don't need to struggle against the Camarilla if you can just cross the &quot;border&quot; and migrate to Anarch land. The same way you don't need to deal with Corporations if you just move to anarchist territory. Again, losing a lot of the setting attractiveness in the way.<br /> <br /> Oh. I am sure that Anarchs are far from perfect. Just like anarchist in Shadowrun (in fact East Berlin is pretty much a hell hole but that's another story). But that doesn't really matter. Back when VTM was Gothic Punk, you could never be free of your elders, never be free of vampiric laws. And the Camarilla (the world state) was the representation of that. Wherever you were, they were too.<br /> That was part of the horror. The Anarch representing the Punk aspect.<br /> <br /> Of course there was the Sabbat... but was freedom really worth that price?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T17:58:40-07:00","id":1440525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440523#post1440523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Or... states.<br /> <br /> That they coexist is the actual issue here. You don't need to struggle against the Camarilla if you can just cross the &quot;border&quot; and migrate to Anarch land. The same way you don't need to deal with Corporations if you just move to anarchist territory. Again, losing a lot of the setting attractiveness in the way.<br /> <br /> Oh. I am sure that Anarchs are far from perfect. Just like anarchist in Shadowrun (in fact East Berlin is pretty much a hell hole but that's another story). But that doesn't really matter. Back when VTM was Gothic Punk, you could never be free of your elders, never be free of vampiric laws. And the Camarilla (the world state) was the representation of that. Wherever you were, they were too.<br /> That was part of the horror. The Anarch representing the Punk aspect.<br /> <br /> Of course there was the Sabbat... but was freedom really worth that price?</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems shockingly assuming the Anarchs are not territorial.<br /> <br /> Which no edition has ever shown.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the struggle for territory is one of the basic elements of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T18:14:35-07:00","id":1440527,"title":"","content":"If you are talking about the Free states or Russia, well Russia fell before the game starts and was not confirmed to be an Anarch regime before... V20, if I recall?<br /> <br /> So we are left with only the Free states as an actual free Anarch territory. And I would argue that the Free states did not subvert the main theme of the game. Just like East Berlin, the Free states was a successful revolution (that happened before) that is slowly slowly losing its stuggle against the establishment whoever they be (Kuey-jin or Camarilla) it's basically the struggle of your local anarch but in a more global way.<br /> <br /> We know the free states are bound to lose. Because this Gothic Punk. The establishment can have setback but they cannot truly lose. What matters is the struggle here. That's the true essence of the resistance. To fight back despite the odds.<br /> <br /> If you are talking about other smaller Anarch pockets. The same rule apply. They only exist because the Camarilla allows them too for whatever political reason. And shall be swiftly crushed when times have changed.<br /> <br /> So again the struggle for territory is fine. What is not fine is the Anarch as an actual alternative to the Camarilla or the Sabbat. Those Anarchs are no longer the punks of VTM. They are something else. Criminals if you insist or New Camarilla, as other call them but Anarch no more.<br /> <br /> If you want to &quot;win&quot; against the Cam. You join the Sabbat. With all the consequence that entails. (and probably lose anyway)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 03-18-2021, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T23:46:11-07:00","id":1440551,"title":"","content":"The issues with the camarilla has always been individual princes (or the councils/methuselah that puppet them). The actual institution itself hasn't been much of a problem. If anything the Camarilla has been a helpful aid to prevent the worst excesses of princes and anarchs. The small-scale Anarchs-within-the-cam made complete sense because they were largely just protesting the policies of the local prince. The first 'anarch' revolt after all wasn't some big conflict with some kind of sect, it was just a revolt against some elders that abused their power. Ditto with the modern era. 'The Camarilla' is just a broad face that makes a good, safe, all-too-general target, while specifically rebelling against 'prince X and elder Y' is grounds for getting you killed<br /> <br /> The issue with V5 is that someone wanted to see everything in terms of 'liberal/progressive' and 'conservative/fascist' and so made the Anarchs more successful than they have any right to be, the Camarilla are something entirely different from what they were, and the Sabbat was carved up for simplicity's sake and had it's most conservative/fascist traits merged into the nuCamarilla (because patriarchal religion is evil conservative stuff, so of course)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T00:32:36-07:00","id":1440556,"title":"","content":"The Anarchs as a faction didn't really exist, as such, previously. You had an attempt at the Anarch free state but it was generally a failure and most &quot;Anarchs&quot; were high generation vampires in a few places who still mostly did what the local Prince wanted while grumbling about it.<br /> <br /> The big thing that changed was that the Gangrel, Brujah and Followers of Set basically all teamed up together, started their own new political faction and usurped the name &quot;Anarch&quot; for themselves. A few of the Gangrel/Brujah/FoS elders might have been in the Anarchs before, but just a tiny bit. Most of them spent decades or centuries in the Camarilla and while they might be part of the &quot;Anarchs&quot; now, I suspect that they see the Anarchs more as an organization that they can control and use to try and vie with the Camarilla, rather than being ideologues and truly believing the precepts of the organization they joined a couple of months ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 03-19-2021, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T00:36:02-07:00","id":1440557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440551#post1440551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with V5 is that someone wanted to see everything in terms of 'liberal/progressive' and 'conservative/fascist' and so made the Anarchs more successful than they have any right to be, the Camarilla are something entirely different from what they were, and the Sabbat was carved up for simplicity's sake and had it's most conservative/fascist traits merged into the nuCamarilla (because patriarchal religion is evil conservative stuff, so of course)</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the biggest problem the Anarchs is that 3 editions made them losers when they should be at least scoring some major successes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440556#post1440556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Anarchs as a faction didn't really exist, as such, previously. You had an attempt at the Anarch free state but it was generally a failure and most &quot;Anarchs&quot; were low generation vampires in a few places who still mostly did what the local Prince wanted.<br /> <br /> The big thing that changed was that the Gangrel, Brujah and Followers of Set basically all teamed up together, started their own new political faction and usurped the name &quot;Anarch&quot; for themselves. A few of the Gangrel/Brujah/FoS elders might have been in the Anarchs before, but just a tiny bit. Most of them spent decades or centuries in the Camarilla and while they might be part of the &quot;Anarchs&quot; now, I suspect that they see the Anarchs more as an organization that they can control and use to try and vie with the Camarilla, rather than being ideologues and truly believing the precepts of the organization they joined a couple of months ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think the Anarchs suffered from &quot;show don't tell.&quot; As soon as the Anarchs were given a personality in Bloodlines, people loved them and wanted to join them.<br /> <br /> La Croix also helped as he was a perfect example of the &quot;Asshole Prince&quot; that had been downplayed since Lodin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T02:05:06-07:00","id":1440564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440557#post1440557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, the biggest problem the Anarchs is that 3 editions made them losers when they should be at least scoring some major successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think they should have ever been winning? Most anarchs just want different guys in charge, or got called an anarch for not toeing the party line as precisely as the prince demands; If they &quot;Won&quot; they'd just reform the local camarilla a bit. The Radicals that want to bring it down are, generally speaking, clowns, overtly self-centered people, and other rejects that don't know how politics work, and who are almost uniformly very young kindred with a few out-of-touch elders inbetween. People who go against the grain are generally less likely to be embraced, as a rule. Oh, and Anarchs infight more than the Camarilla, which is hilarious given how much smaller they are. <br /> So, I ask again, why do you think they should have been winning? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> La Croix also helped as he was a perfect example of the &quot;Asshole Prince&quot; that had been downplayed since Lodin. </div> </div> </div>LaCroix was a clown. A Ventrue with a Charisma of 1. He was depicted as somewhat of an anomaly among princes. <br /> Mind you, maybe I have high standards; I don't see how anyone could've liked Nines, Damsel, or Vietnam. (eh, skelter's not so bad so long as you don't question his beliefs... which makes him pretty shitty really.) The Best Anarch was the Baron, and he was more the prince than Lacroix. <br /> The more I play/read, the more I think the Cam are a good deal. I don't know, maybe something set you off or struck a cord when you were younger and now you're fixated on anarch victory. Me? My Vampire-views are comfortably distant from my real-world-politic views. So I can say the Cam (before v5 at least) was the only realistic option, while not hurting my RL want of a fully automated luxury gay space communism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T02:14:18-07:00","id":1440565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440564#post1440564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> while not hurting my RL want of a fully automated luxury gay space communism.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ahh Eclipse Phase Technosocialism <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T03:18:08-07:00","id":1440572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440507#post1440507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the anarchs make real equality, modern systems of government, the democratic process, and freedom from Blood Bonds look easy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely what makes the anarchs the most boring faction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T03:27:12-07:00","id":1440573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440572#post1440572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Precisely what makes the anarchs the most boring faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the problem is they're boring, then you're doing them wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T05:34:02-07:00","id":1440580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440573#post1440573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the problem is they're boring, then you're doing them wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> well, they were pretty damn dull in Bloodlines, which is where I am told they were at their best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T06:35:38-07:00","id":1440585,"title":"","content":"Anarchs are righteous. That's why they cannot be winner. Not in the Wod, not in Vampires. Or we are not talking about Vampire: The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> So either the Anarchs lose their righteousness to &quot;win&quot; becoming in the process a watered down version of the Sabbat or the Camarilla. (they basically are both from the little I read of V5). Or they don't lose anything, and you now play a bad guy vs good guy kind of game with some touch of darkness so the good guy here gets a more &quot;anti-hero&quot; edge than your standard lawful good faction.<br /> But still clearly good when you compare them to the eldritch horror that hides the Camarilla and Sabbat closets.<br /> <br /> Both options are just terrible in my view. But it is what is.<br /> <br /> It is also why the Sabbat as we knew can no longer exist. Not as long as the Anarch literally took their place. Both in the &quot;cold&quot; war. And as the alternative playable faction. To say nothing of the redistribution of the Sabbat's themes inside the new Red and Blue factions.<br /> <br /> Frankly the only way the Sabbat is salvageable in V5 writeup is by making them an Anarch sub-faction. (or at least the loyalist/moderate are) Subverting the Anarch from the inside and waiting to break away or absorb the Anarchs when the Inquisition crisis in done and the ultra-conservative return from their crusades.<br /> <br /> The Anarch Sabbat also has the advantage of creating many interesting conflict in the overstretched Anarch movement while making the reunification of the Sabbat an uphill battle for whomever the task will fall upon. (I can already imagine a campaign based on just that!)<br /> <br /> That's the only way the Sabbat can still exist as a faction in NA without some big retcons at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 03-19-2021, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T07:32:12-07:00","id":1440592,"title":"","content":"I think I'd quite like it if the Sabbat do get the big kicking that's been shown so far go back to being the monsters in bedtime stories. The whole idea of two or three big factions having a global war always felt a bit weird and out of touch with the basic setting.<br /> I'd much rather have the camarilla as a distributed, badly connected network of domains that can call on help from each other if needed, but aren't usually in regular communication. On the edges of this you have the anarchs, who are usually ancilla blowing off steam for a couple of decades until they grow up, someone with connections poaches their turf, or they run into something scary and need backup.<br /> Outside this you have everything else, Sabbat, baali, werewolves, cities run run by elders with terrifying levels of dominate, a commune of democratic vampires who would never claim to be aligned with &quot;anarchs&quot; and so on.<br /> However I know lots of people like the Sabbat and the free States, so accept I'm on to a loser <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25078-brickman","name":"Brickman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T13:28:35-07:00","id":1440629,"title":"","content":"I've always seen it as the Cam having 70% of cities. non-sectarian holdouts and independent clans make up 15% (most independents are going to hold baronies, not entire cities) sabbat make 9% and anarchs take the remaining 1% (again, most 'anarch' territories are really just outskirts the prince doesn't bother to control) <br /> <br /> A thing that bothers me about the anarchs is the term Baron. <br /> Like, what the Sabbat are doing with their lords-spiritual hierarchy makes a lot of sense. <br /> But the Anarchs are defining their leaders with a title of nobility? Even if 'Baron' was a low-tier title sometimes auctioned off to merchants, that'd make it more an appropriate title to give to a Settite or Giovanni who wants to take up and govern a territory in your city. Anarchs being all anti-feudal and such should never adopt the title. <br /> <br /> But, eh, if we wanna get into this, I think most Camarilla princes would better call themselves Dukes or Marquises and it doesn't have as good of a ring. Plus all those titles get a bit antsy when two &quot;princes&quot; meet and one's given himself a higher title than the other... <br /> Maybe &quot;prince&quot;, like harpy, was originally a disparaging title. <br /> Maybe, if we want to re-organize titles to be more coherent (I don't actually want to) The Justicars would be dukes, and the princes would be marquises or counts, and then... <br /> <br /> The Sabbat actually win for having the best Title system. The Tremere get points for structure, but not for titles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T13:39:04-07:00","id":1440631,"title":"","content":"Isn't &quot;prince&quot; supposed to have a more classical connotation than a feudal, medieval one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T13:44:08-07:00","id":1440633,"title":"","content":"Well, I disagree with a lot of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440509#post1440509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it's Gothic PUNK.<br /> <br /> The whole point is being a rebel against the Man. The Anarchs are the Edgerunner faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>The punk portion is basically an aesthetic, and while its one that should be included in the game, it should not be the only one. And it's one I personally feel is childish and unappealing. Most players that I know agree with me. But it's also one that one of my best friends, who I met while playing Vampire, likes. And he's very pro-Anarch obviously. So it's fine to be part of the game, but I think defining the game by it is a mistake. The Lost Boys is an entertaining movie, but it doesn't define the genre.<br /> <br /> It's a legitimate choice for players, but its primarily aesthetic, not moral.<br /> <br /> If I had to define my own style of play and running games, I would call it Gothic-Noir.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440509#post1440509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IAlso, just because they're the moral faction doesn't mean they're the one people want to play. Not everyone wants to be the good guy, especially in a game where you are a traditional fantasy monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never seen the Anarch as the &quot;moral&quot; faction. They just use certain kind of rhetoric. That you may like that rhetoric doesn't mean it has anything substantial to do with the actual group. The Jacobins and Bolsheviks had a lot of good propaganda, both were far morally worse than the groups they replaced. They were Dostoevsky's Grand Inquisitor on steroids.<br /> <br /> You have the dirt bag criminals or cynical exploiters using the Anarch label. Less moral than the Camarilla in general. Equally repulsive as the Camarilla's worst.<br /> <br /> You have Anarchs who basically want the same system, but with themselves in charge since then think they'd do it &quot;better&quot;. In most cases, that would not be true. They'd either be just as bad, or make such a muck of it they'd be removed from power. Depending on how many corpses they create, they're either just equally moral or less moral than the Camarilla. This is probably an honest assessment of Maldavis.<br /> <br /> Then you have the naive fools who are sincere in doing morally better, but utterly unprepared for actual rule. In theory this group is morally better, but would make such a mess of things, in practice it's a wash or morally worse. Good intentions are not enough to be moral. Consequences of your actions matter.<br /> <br /> Then you have the failed idealists. People who originally started morally better, but quickly became so angry that they gleefully adopted all the tactics of the enemy (and even worse) that was supposed to have been the reasons they opposed them in the first place. I think this is likely where we disagree because this is where I'd likely put Anita Wainwright who always reminded me of the Weather Underground types so distraught over violence that they mail bombs to people and devolve into terrorism. I consider them to be morally worse than average because they're committing the same crimes they are supposedly railing against, but don't even realize what has happened to them.<br /> <br /> Then there's the existential drama queen who creates problems because reacting to them and claiming oppression gives them personal meaning in life. But they are just obnoxious trolls. But they can fool a lot of naive people until they learn better. Equivalent people exist in the Camarilla. So its a wash again.<br /> <br /> There are the sad sack victims of society. People who honestly didn't do anything, but somehow became on someone's shit list. Caitiffs. Thin bloods. Social misfits. People in the wrong place and at the wrong time. Bad luck of the draw. These people may not necessarily be morally better, but they're definitely victims who are sympathies go out too. Unfortunately, some of these will become victims regardless of who is in charge. One portion of them won't be the victims in a new regime, but some other group will exchange places with them. As individuals, they may draw on our moral sympathies, but collectively it does not mean they are morally better simply because they are the losers of vampire society.<br /> <br /> Then there are the Well Meaning Morons or Useful Idiots. They're sincere saps who actually believe the rhetoric of the cynical exploiters, would-be Princes and the rest. They too will simply be used as cannon fodder or eaten by the Revolution. As individuals I can consider them to be morally better, extremely stupid, and doing great harm as they allow themselves to be exploited. But many PC Anarchs probably fit this category. Eventually those who survive will realize the Anarchs are just as big as a Racket as the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Lastly you have serious, sincere vampires who want continued reform of the system to produce a better form of vampire government, but doing that outside the system. Probably morally better. But this does not really distinguish them from vampires of the same ilk who remain committed to do it inside the Camarilla without using the violence of the Anarchs. So it's really a wash when comparing Anarchs versus Camarilla.<br /> <br /> So I never considered the Anarchs to be more moral even in theory as opposed to practice. They just have more sympathetic propaganda to a certain kind of people, and likely have a higher percentage of people who want to be more moral simply because they are younger and more in touch with their Humanity. But it's a wash. While individual Anarchs might be &quot;good people&quot;, you can find them in the Camarilla too. And neither group is profoundly influenced by any moral leaders of their kind.<br /> <br /> Conclaves are an under represented tool of Camarilla society. The game doesn't utilize them much, and we don't hear a lot about their decisions and how it influences the Camarilla. For many chronicles, they may not even exist at all. But I think it they are utilized in game, it enables people to let off steam, allows slow reforms by building up consensus, and keeps the most tyrannical Princes and elders in checks. Not enough to satisfy everyone, but well enough that it keeps the Camarilla viable and allows many &quot;Anarchs&quot; to rejoin the system after they become more experienced, wiser, or simply jaded and exhausted. I think Conclaves are extremely important to the setting, and explain a lot of elements people may otherwise find anomalous.<br /> <br /> In so far there is a moral faction within Vampire, it is not based around vampire politics. Its spiritual seekers of Golconda who have progressed far along that path, and likely do their best to minimize their involvement in vampire society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T14:41:16-07:00","id":1440638,"title":"","content":"Ultimately I've never seen the Anarchs as a realistic group. Their goal is to rebel against the status quo, but even if they won they'd pretty quickly become indistinguishable from the Camarilla. You'd still have a Masquerade. Individual cities would still have their leader telling other people what to do. You'd still have some sort of interconnected organization empowering local leaders and helping them to uphold the Masquerade. And considering the way vampires work, in which lower generation, older vampires are generally stronger, smarter, wealthier, and all around more capable than younger vampires, you'd still end up with older vampires in positions of leadership.<br /> <br /> Even the Sabbat, which hates the Camarilla ended up with more or less exactly the same system, the only difference really being the Vaulderie, which helps to maintain a slightly more equitable bond between all members, from ancient elders to the youngest shovelhead, but even then just a small one.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the Camarilla are a bunch of dicks, but that's because <i>vampires</i> are dicks who have to struggle to pretend to be human. And whether the Anarchs were in control or the Camarilla, that much isn't going to change. The new boss would be the same big dick the old boss was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T15:40:44-07:00","id":1440650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440638#post1440638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately I've never seen the Anarchs as a realistic group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually argue they're inevitable for the exact reasons you oppose them.<br /> <br /> When the leaders of a society that horde wealth, territory, and power will not grow old and die out then the people underneath them will MAKE openings above them.<br /> <br /> That's the very cynical but axiomatic reality of Anarchs.<br /> <br /> There will always be people who rail against the tyranny of Elders, WILL kill them, and WILL become exactly as bad.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T16:19:11-07:00","id":1440659,"title":"","content":"It's funny because I actually feel like I'm the guy who has the much more nasty position on the Anarchs than a lot of the posters here. I certainly don't feel like they're the good guys and I actually was in the process of writing a lengthy speech about it before <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> pretty much summarized a lot of my points.<br /> <br /> Still, I recommend people check out my TOP TEN TIPS TO PLAYING ANARCHS blog entry.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2020/04/ten-tips-to-playing-anarchs.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://unitedfederationofcharles.blo...g-anarchs.html</a><br /> <br /> One sample that's relevant:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>1:] Anarchs are not the good guys</b><br /> <br /> An important thing to understanding the appeal of the Anarchs in a Gothic Punk world is that it is shades of gray and black, never white (at least among vampires). The first Anarch ever introduced was Forged in Steel's Juggler. Juggler was a hypocrite to the Anarch cause who manipulated, lied, and cheated Neonates in much the same way as his Camarilla counterpart Modius. He even had his own Blood Bound female minion, Evelyn, exactly like the Prince. The Anarchs are not the Rebel Alliance and whenever they do take over a territory like Los Angeles or Berlin, it's a crapshot whether that territory will become better or worse for their influence. Being an Anarch means you're against the city's Elders and Prince, nothing more or less.<br /> <br /> <b>2:] Anarchs<i> think </i>they're the good guys</b><br /> <br /> Contradicting number 1# is the fact that many anarchs believe themselves to be the good guys or, at least, the lesser evil. Everything is relative in Cainite society and the fury over past injustices is a major reason why the Movement has not died in six hundred years. There are many idealistic voices among the Anarchs like Maldavis, Anita Wainwright, Jeremy MacNeil, Nines, and Salvador Garcia. Don't get me wrong, they're still ****ing vampires but they have legitimate greviances motivating them as well as a passionate belief things can get better. It's the presence of these individuals that prevents the entire Anarch experiment from being written off as just another bunch of Kindred warring for territory. </div> </div> </div>Anarchs are an inevitability of Kindred society because the only way to survive in Kindred society is to push back when you're being pushed by vampire society. Younger vampires have an advantage over Elders in the fact they're willing to team up and risk their lives in a way that the older members of vampiredom won't. Also, the advancement of technology and (slightly) higher humanity means that even if they're just awake an hour ahead of an Elder that's a fucking hour of vulnerability.<br /> <br /> (I always felt 'Wake With Morning's Freshness&quot; was ridiculously overpowered as a result)<br /> <br /> Now this may seem like a cynical non-idealistic interpretation of the Anarchs but I turn to ASSASSINS CREED 3 for how to define them. The Anarchs are the Assassins in that they're ostensibly all for freedom but also hypocritically make decisions for the public in the same way as the Templars as well as strike randomly outward versus a more targeted approach. In AC 3, it's even more underscored. The founding fathers are fighting for THEIR freedom but not EVERYONE's freedom (see Native Americans, the fact they're slavers).<br /> <br /> Most Anarchs don't give a shit for Kine or their freedom. In fact, they're actually WORSE because the Camarilla's laws about Domain and Execution mean that humans get fed on less overall.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs have that unhappy medium between the Camarilla and the Sabbat where they're all about FREEDOM and fighting the power but have enough people appalled by the Beast not to fall to it completely but are just a hair's breadth away from ending up corrupted into something worse than what they're fighting. The Ministry joining the &quot;Second Anarch Revolt&quot; is a sign of the Anarchs likely going down the same road as the First One.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-19-2021, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T03:17:56-07:00","id":1440702,"title":"","content":"I pretty much agree with everything you've got in there and as you say there's not a lot of difference between your view and Black Fox's.<br /> Where I think I see it differently though is the idea that's there's a worthwhile &quot;Faction&quot; called the anarchs. Sure elders get toppled and new domains set up trying their own style of governance, but they're not part of some worldwide organisation. They're so fractured between these idealists, criminals and so on that they could never pose a serious threat and would either fold back into the cam within a few decades, or sit on the fringes being a cool oddball town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25078-brickman","name":"Brickman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T09:47:30-07:00","id":1440726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440551#post1440551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issues with the camarilla has always been individual princes (or the councils/methuselah that puppet them). The actual institution itself hasn't been much of a problem. If anything the Camarilla has been a helpful aid to prevent the worst excesses of princes and anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's another distinction that is easily lost when the game focuses too much on the conflict between the anarchs and the Camarilla: the princes are not synonymous with the Camarilla. In many instances, the princes are <i>antagonistic</i> to the Camarilla. <i>&quot;Historically, there have been many attempts by the leaders of the Camarilla to assert more authority over other aspects of vampiric existence. Each time, the attempt has failed in a wave of bloodshed. <b>The princes do not brook interference into what they consider to be their historical rights and privileges</b>, nor do the Methuselahs desire a competitor who could thwart their aims. Therefore, <b>the Camarilla remains a divided sect of only moderate influence</b>.&quot;</i> (<i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> 2nd Edition, page 42; emphases mine.)<br /> <br /> You could as easily focus on the types of people, anarch or otherwise, who would want to work <i>with</i> the Camarilla to curb the excesses of individual princes. This was at least a possible if not a likely avenue for reform in earlier editions of the game. When you completely separate the anarchs from the Camarilla, like the recent iterations of the game seem to have been keen on doing, it makes for what I consider a poorer and less nuanced setting, not a richer one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T09:55:23-07:00","id":1440728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brickman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440702#post1440702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where I think I see it differently though is the idea that's there's a worthwhile &quot;Faction&quot; called the anarchs. Sure elders get toppled and new domains set up trying their own style of governance, but they're not part of some worldwide organisation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really the core of the disagreement. Anarchs make sense to me when they enjoy the protection of the Camarilla but want to see a change in how the majority of Camarilla cities are governed. They do not make sense to me as an independent organization that has severed its ties with the Camarilla and wants to see it destroyed.<br /> <br /> To take just one example of what it would mean to be truly without the support of the Camarilla, consider the Masquerade. The Camarilla is the global conspiracy to hide the existence of vampires from mortal knowledge. This is what the sect was founded to do, and what remains its primary concern 500 years later. In addition to directly protecting all its members from discovery on a nightly basis, the Camarilla indirectly protects every single vampire on the planet, <i>including even the Sabbat.</i> Not out of the goodness of their hearts, but because they have to, in order for the Masquerade to function.<br /> <br /> To say that the preservation of the Masquerade is not an easy task would be an understatement. For many players, it strained credibility even before the era of smartphones and the internet. The Masquerade is the central conceit that you have to accept in order to enjoy the setting. I can suspend my disbelief <i>if</i> the entity responsible for upholding the Masquerade is global, incredibly wealthy, and influential beyond measure in the mortal world. Something like a 500-year-old organization that has dedicated unfathomable resources to the task.<br /> <br /> When the Anarch Movement swaggers onto the stage as an independent alternative to the Camarilla, what I want to know is where did the resources, the connections, the institutional knowledge, the numbers, the <i>everything</i> that is necessary to maintain and promulgate the Masquerade on their turf come from. If the anarchs <i>still</i> depend on the Camarilla's resources to repair the vast majority of Masquerade breaches, well... There's a reason why people say that hypocrisy is the worst offense of all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T10:00:37-07:00","id":1440730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440726#post1440726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's another distinction that is easily lost when the game focuses too much on the conflict between the anarchs and the Camarilla: the princes are not synonymous with the Camarilla. In many instances, the princes are <i>antagonistic</i> to the Camarilla. <i>&quot;Historically, there have been many attempts by the leaders of the Camarilla to assert more authority over other aspects of vampiric existence. Each time, the attempt has failed in a wave of bloodshed. <b>The princes do not brook interference into what they consider to be their historical rights and privileges</b>, nor do the Methuselahs desire a competitor who could thwart their aims. Therefore, <b>the Camarilla remains a divided sect of only moderate influence</b>.&quot;</i> (<i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> 2nd Edition, page 42; emphases mine.)<br /> <br /> You could as easily focus on the types of people, anarch or otherwise, who would want to work <i>with</i> the Camarilla to curb the excesses of individual princes. This was at least a possible if not a likely avenue for reform in earlier editions of the game. When you completely separate the anarchs from the Camarilla, like the recent iterations of the game seem to have been keen on doing, it makes for what I consider a poorer and less nuanced setting, not a richer one.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting pursuit and one I find more morally sympathetic than typical Anarch goals, but I don't see how the existence of completely separate Anarchs eliminates it as a possibility, even if it may make it more difficult.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T11:42:21-07:00","id":1440738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440659#post1440659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. The founding fathers are fighting for THEIR freedom but not EVERYONE's freedom (see Native Americans, the fact they're slavers).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Always remember that John Wilkes Booth said &quot;sic semper tyrannis&quot;, which is to &quot;thus always to tyrants&quot; with a complete lack of irony when he assassinated Lincoln. He meant it, because from his perspective Lincoln was destroying the resources that gave real human beings freedom, and was doing it for petty control freak reasons. The Anarchs mean much the same thing when they talk about &quot;freedom&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T23:09:51-07:00","id":1440811,"title":"","content":"It seems that White Wolf has confirmed they are bringing back PATHS OF ENLIGHTENMENT so <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25011\" data-vbnamecard=\"25011\">Taggie</a> should be happy.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/development-blog-defining-clans\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/development-blog-defining-clans</a><br /> <br /> <b><i>Essential Experience</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>From a design perspective, the function of these clans (and the other factions to come\u2026) is to create expectations for the players. Each helps define what a Kindred of that particular clan might expect to do in stories.</i><br /> <br /> <i>For Vampire, we describe these essential experiences using the statement \u201cthe vampire as X.\u201d The Brujah are the vampire as rebel, the Toreador are the vampire as seducer, the Banu Haqim are the vampire as judge, and so on.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Since characters act on the world, whether they\u2019re players\u2019 characters or Storyteller characters, every faction is designed to do something that\u2019s expressed by verbs. That\u2019s one of the big distinctions between designing for interactive media like games and designing for traditional media in which the \u201caudience\u201d doesn\u2019t have input into what\u2019s happening. Players verb.</i><br /> <br /> <i>(You\u2019ll see these as other titles in the World of Darkness take shape, as well, from the <b>Sabbat\u2019s Paths of Enlightenment</b> to <b>Werewolf\u2019s tribes</b>.)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T02:20:57-07:00","id":1440816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brickman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440702#post1440702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I pretty much agree with everything you've got in there and as you say there's not a lot of difference between your view and Black Fox's.<br /> Where I think I see it differently though is the idea that's there's a worthwhile &quot;Faction&quot; called the anarchs. Sure elders get toppled and new domains set up trying their own style of governance, but they're not part of some worldwide organisation. They're so fractured between these idealists, criminals and so on that they could never pose a serious threat and would either fold back into the cam within a few decades, or sit on the fringes being a cool oddball town.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see Anarchs existing as a faction coming from both sides of things generally:<br /> <br /> 1. Younger vampires team up together and have an informal network that actually doesn't really EXIST until the Anarch Free States and the continued pressure of the Camarilla FORCES it to exist. Prior to 5th Edition, the Anarchs really were a political party that happened to have one or two violent civil wars within the Camarilla and some separatist locations that served as a release valve for dissident Kindred.<br /> <br /> 2. Elders basically had a habit of blaming any redictivist or nonconformist Kindred as &quot;Anarchs&quot; and this ironically is why modern rebel Kindred are called Anarchs. Basically, they got called it enough that they adopt the name of it.<br /> <br /> Generally, the theme of Elders vs. Anarchs is that the Elders keep squeezing the latter until they form into a brutal insurgency.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla is pathologically incapable of learning, &quot;It is better to be feared than loved if a Prince cannot be both but above all he must not be HATED.&quot; The Camarilla has deep trouble with that latter one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T12:29:31-07:00","id":1440846,"title":"","content":"I suspect that's an inevitable part of them warring with other elders.<br /> <br /> It's kind of like in athletics. Athletes tend to be physically ruined by the end of their careers, because the only way you win is by being willing to push your body past the limits of its design, and to do so again and again. The guys not willing to do that lose.<br /> <br /> Elders beat elders by pushing all of their resources to the limit and beyond. In the back of its mind, the elder knows that this will anger those who serve it. And maybe it even feels bad about that if it cares about its progeny. But this military thing has to be done NOW NOW NOW or it will lose to the elder who IS willing to push its progeny to do those dangerous things NOW NOW NOW. It probably thinks, well, if we lose, my progeny are dead anyway, and if we win, I can always make it up to the survivors with gifts.<br /> <br /> So let's say you have a situation where the elder has three progeny, and he pushes them to do something that gets two of them killed, and causes the survivor to have suffered multiple aggravated wounds, and to have lost both his ghouls. The survivor liked his fellow progeny, and he liked his ghouls. In fact, he was planning to embrace his ghouls one day. And so the elder calls him in, and rewards him with money, and this really delicious kine he bought from the Circulatory System.<br /> <br /> Now in the elder's mind, its done as much as it could. It only pushed them to do things that absolutely had to be done or they were all dead anyway. And its rewarded the survivor with the best it could afford, what with so many resources having been destroyed in the war with that other elder. It thinks everything is fine and dandy.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the progeny is looking at his or her reward, and thinking about all (s)he has lost, and thinking &quot;fuuuuuuuuuuuck yoooooouuuu!!!!!!!!!!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T14:21:00-07:00","id":1440859,"title":"","content":"Lol let's water the clans down to verbs because reading an entire book is hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T11:35:38-07:00","id":1441400,"title":"","content":"My ideal treatment of the Sabbat would be to give them a proper update to V5 and neither roll back the clock on them or make them too different from Revised.<br /> <br /> * Have them lose Montreal and Mexico City<br /> * Have a large chunk of them been fighting the Gehenna Crusade (and not embarrass themselves)<br /> * Have the Lasombra defection acknowledged<br /> * Have them have an official policy on the Second Inquisition and changes in teh Masquerade<br /> * Have them have to deal with a United Anarchs<br /> * Have them lose the Harbingers<br /> * Have them deal with the upswing in Noddism and Blood Cults<br /> * Have them acknowledge Drowned Legacies<br /> <br /> BUT<br /> <br /> * Also have them have remaining territory<br /> * Acknowledge the Paths of Enlightenment<br /> * Have them acknowledge House Goratrix (which means they have their own Antediluvian)<br /> * Have them have destroyed LOTS of Elders and Methuselahs in the Middle East<br /> * Have them holding their own against all the factions like the Drowned Legacies, SI, and so on<br /> * Make options for playable Sabbat<br /> * Incorporate options for all varieties of Sabbat playstyles and antagonists<br /> * Reintroduce the Salubri Antitribu and Kisayd<br /> * Show the new Regent and end the Civil War<br /> * DON'T make the number of Monty Coven secret methusalehs any more than a handful of plotters<br /> <br /> I mean, the Sabbat has taken some lumps yes but are they ANY worse off than the Camarilla or Anarchs at this point? I mean, let's face it, the Camarilla lost the Tremere Inner Council and two Clans in the past twenty years.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat lost Montreal and Mexico City....but the Camarilla lost London, Vienna, and Berlin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T11:45:14-07:00","id":1441401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440811#post1440811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems that White Wolf has confirmed they are bringing back PATHS OF ENLIGHTENMENT so <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25011\" data-vbnamecard=\"25011\">Taggie</a> should be happy.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/development-blog-defining-clans\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/development-blog-defining-clans</a><br /> <br /> <b><i>Essential Experience</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>From a design perspective, the function of these clans (and the other factions to come\u2026) is to create expectations for the players. Each helps define what a Kindred of that particular clan might expect to do in stories.</i><br /> <br /> <i>For Vampire, we describe these essential experiences using the statement \u201cthe vampire as X.\u201d The Brujah are the vampire as rebel, the Toreador are the vampire as seducer, the Banu Haqim are the vampire as judge, and so on.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Since characters act on the world, whether they\u2019re players\u2019 characters or Storyteller characters, every faction is designed to do something that\u2019s expressed by verbs. That\u2019s one of the big distinctions between designing for interactive media like games and designing for traditional media in which the \u201caudience\u201d doesn\u2019t have input into what\u2019s happening. Players verb.</i><br /> <br /> <i>(You\u2019ll see these as other titles in the World of Darkness take shape, as well, from the <b>Sabbat\u2019s Paths of Enlightenment</b> to <b>Werewolf\u2019s tribes</b>.)</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Totally depends on how they handle them. If they are lore sheets, or interact with Tenets and Convictions, then nope. Also not a fan of what the verb system has done to some of the clans, like totally destroy their established lore and identity. So I have no faith what so ever that the paths will be anything better","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 03-25-2021, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T12:11:56-07:00","id":1441405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1441401#post1441401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Totally depends on how they handle them. If they are lore sheets, or interact with Tenets and Convictions, then nope. Also not a fan of what the verb system has done to some of the clans, like totally destroy their established lore and identity. So I have no faith what so ever that the paths will be anything better</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you're bound to be disappointed because they're not getting rid of Tenets and Convictions. That's there until the end of 5th Edition and probably beyond.<br /> <br /> Sorry man.<br /> <br /> I was hoping you might find something you liked about it but if it's a lost cause, it's better to acknowledge it and move on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-25-2021, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T12:21:13-07:00","id":1441407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1441405#post1441405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then you're bound to be disappointed because they're not getting rid of Tenets and Convictions. That's there until the end of 5th Edition and probably beyond.<br /> <br /> Sorry man.<br /> <br /> I was hoping you might find something you liked about it but if it's a lost cause, it's better to acknowledge it and move on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair. I flat hate the entire concept of morality and self control as an external thing, I find the entire idea morally reprehensible and repugnant, it's far to close to 'the devil made me do it' which is a malicious at best attempt to ditch responsibility, and V5 has enshrined that excuse of abusers as a core mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T12:36:43-07:00","id":1441408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1441407#post1441407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Fair. I flat hate the entire concept of morality and self control as an external thing, I find the entire idea morally reprehensible and repugnant, it's far to close to 'the devil made me do it' which is a malicious at best attempt to ditch responsibility, and V5 has enshrined that excuse of abusers as a core mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've made your opinion abundantly clear and I've expressed my disagreement. I doubt either of us will change each other's mind.<br /> <br /> Time to discuss other things I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T12:41:00-07:00","id":1441409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1441408#post1441408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You've made your opinion abundantly clear and I've expressed my disagreement. I doubt either of us will change each other's mind.<br /> <br /> Time to discuss other things I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T00:44:46-07:00","id":1441474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1440859#post1440859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lol let's water the clans down to verbs because reading an entire book is hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see why they did it. But in my view, you distill down to a single verb to then build back up to the complexity that a splat needs. The great thing about the Clans is that each holds multitudes. You lose a lot if you refine too much.<br /> <br /> I mentioned a Tolkienesque way of worldbuilding before--where you present a mix of truths, half-truths and untruths, and where the accounts of what's happening and happened are all partial and biased--and that was always a strength of the WoD. So you need Clans that have key themes but also that are able to subvert those same themes: a Baali Christian crusader wanting to purge the Infernal, say, or a Kiasyd fascist who burns books and steals knowledge they deem to be dangerous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T18:10:05-07:00","id":1441586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1441474#post1441474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you need Clans that have key themes but also that are able to subvert those same themes: <b>a Baali Christian crusader wanting to purge the Infernal</b>, say, or a Kiasyd fascist who burns books and steals knowledge they deem to be dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm generally a fan of characters stepping out from under the tyranny of clan stereotypes, but I think circumstances wherein the bolded character would survive to reach independence would be exceedingly rare.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T18:34:46-07:00","id":1441589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1441586#post1441586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm generally a fan of characters stepping out from under the tyranny of clan stereotypes, but I think circumstances wherein the bolded character would survive to reach independence would be exceedingly rare.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I could see a pretty easy one where the Baali decides to Embrace a warrior of True Faith to break him, only to get murdered by said soldier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T00:13:05-07:00","id":1441614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1441589#post1441589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could see a pretty easy one where the Baali decides to Embrace a warrior of True Faith to break him, only to get murdered by said soldier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too. Also, the Baali is pretty fractured in the Final Nights, so it's not like the Camarilla or Sabbst Inquisition, where they can throw everything at hunting down a rogue agent. <br /> <br /> The Molochim wouldn't necessarily destroy such a character outright, either, since their whole schtick is that they do evil to prevent even worse evil--and they hunt down and destroy the Nergali for being the wrong kind of infernalists.<br /> <br /> Said Christian crusader, anti-infernalist Baali could also pose as Tremere, due to the similarity of their blood. They don't need to declare who and what they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T14:09:49-07:00","id":1441699,"title":"","content":"One thing I've noticed is that the Predator types, other than Alleycat, don't really work with Sabbat. How would you handle it with Sabbat? I've been considering replacing Predator-type with something Path related, or simply dumping Predator-type altogether and simply making the Sabbat discipline spread 1 dot in two clan discipline, and 2 dots in one clan discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T15:50:56-07:00","id":1441714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1441699#post1441699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I've noticed is that the Predator types, other than Alleycat, don't really work with Sabbat. How would you handle it with Sabbat? I've been considering replacing Predator-type with something Path related, or simply dumping Predator-type altogether and simply making the Sabbat discipline spread 1 dot in two clan discipline, and 2 dots in one clan discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, I assume most Sabbat feed when they want where they want and forego any sort of real care. Still, I wouldn't be surprised if they do some NON-Boogeyman Sabbat too.<br /> <br /> Sabbat who have normal unlives outside of Jyhad like Sienna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T12:35:34-07:00","id":1441796,"title":"","content":"First, the majority of Sabbat generally feed the same as the Cam; Nailing someone's grandmother to the roof and feeding from her feet might be done now and then, but it's too much of a pain in the ass to do on the regular. Give me Convenience or give me death. You should also consider that, unless V5 deletes the viniculum, Sabbat need to consider their pack when they want to do something troublesome and stupid. <br /> Second, Predator types don't actually work, Sabbat or not.. Good idea, bad execution. <br /> <br /> First, for whatever reason, V5 has established you learn Disciplines through resonances rather than using them. Predator types run contrary to that. <br /> Second, it's pretty rare someone so dedicates themselves to a predator type. At least, predator types that aren't sandman or cassanova or prisoner abuse. Ventrue,Salubri, Giovanni and thinbloods are often exceptions, but most of the 'predator types' are really, really bad ideas to do on a regular basis. Alleycat feedings should be crimes of opportunity, not your standard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T12:38:26-07:00","id":1441798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1441796#post1441796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, the majority of Sabbat generally feed the same as the Cam; Nailing someone's grandmother to the roof and feeding from her feet might be done now and then, but it's too much of a pain in the ass to do on the regular. Give me Convenience or give me death. You should also consider that, unless V5 deletes the viniculum, Sabbat need to consider their pack when they want to do something troublesome and stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with most of your post but this is a bizarre hot take.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat ENCOURAGES massacres and slaughter among Packs as a way of binding you together as well as reducing your connection to your Humanity. There's literally dozens of games described that involve murder, mayhem, and atrocity. These are things the Sabbat do as sports. The Camarilla doesn't have kidnapping mortals, brainwashing them, releasing them into a mall and then hunting them for sport.<br /> <br /> Not everyone is Vykos.<br /> <br /> Most are soccer hooligans.<br /> <br /> And even Vykos enjoys the occasional game of head soccer.<br /> <br /> &quot;Football,&quot; - My Brujah Antitribu","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-28-2021, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T13:11:34-07:00","id":1441803,"title":"","content":"It seems like the predator types were designed as a plug-n-play mechanic that was both faster and harder to abuse than the old Flaws+Freebies-Merits system. But the result is only useful in completely bog-standard Camarilla games. The Sabbat would just murder the Siren's spurned lover or jealous partner, for example.<br /> <br /> I've seen some homebrew predator types that might work, but that was on an old computer and I don't know where to find them anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T13:17:18-07:00","id":1441805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1441796#post1441796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, the majority of Sabbat generally feed the same as the Cam; Nailing someone's grandmother to the roof and feeding from her feet might be done now and then, but it's too much of a pain in the ass to do on the regular. Give me Convenience or give me death. You should also consider that, unless V5 deletes the viniculum, Sabbat need to consider their pack when they want to do something troublesome and stupid.<br /> Second, Predator types don't actually work, Sabbat or not.. Good idea, bad execution.<br /> <br /> First, for whatever reason, V5 has established you learn Disciplines through resonances rather than using them. Predator types run contrary to that.<br /> Second, it's pretty rare someone so dedicates themselves to a predator type. At least, predator types that aren't sandman or cassanova or prisoner abuse. Ventrue,Salubri, Giovanni and thinbloods are often exceptions, but most of the 'predator types' are really, really bad ideas to do on a regular basis. Alleycat feedings should be crimes of opportunity, not your standard.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's an odd take on feeding, alley cat ambushes, kidnappings, blood games etc are fairly standard, and part of why Sabbat cities have insane murder rates.... Sure don't tear apart the mayor outside the town hall but round up an entire encampment of rough sleepers, make them fight, eat the losers and embrace the winners? That's some quality entertainment, or hunt someone you deem to be strong, spend hours or nights tracking them, and draining them at the end? Feral Heart is all aboard that idea...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T14:01:46-07:00","id":1441808,"title":"","content":"Every member of the Sabbat ritually killing on average a person about once a season gives you a high murder rate. Those Sabbat killing people every night or even once a week doesn't give you a high-murder rate, it makes your city a concentration camp. <br /> <br /> This is average speaking. I'm sure you've got once-a-month killers and avoids-killing vampires among the sabbat. Three things you should consider: <br /> 1- Sabbat generally fuck with the masquerade in enemy territory, and don't really try as hard to shit in their own backyard. <br /> 2- A lot of the Sabbat's sick fuckery can be done without killing people; Extremely unethical 'pranks' and such. You chase a man for sport, but you only maim him. <br /> 3- A lot of the Sabbat's sick fuckery are really just vampire employee team-building exercises, and you can share a murder throughout the whole pack, you don't need to kill one person each. <br /> <br /> <br /> IDK about you lot, but even if I was a psycho sabbat, I'd still get pissed off about someone in my pack going so overboard that it drew hunter attention to me. Someone's going to monomancy the fool for the good of the pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T14:09:51-07:00","id":1441809,"title":"","content":"True. For example, digging up a corpse from the graveyard, sneaking it into someone's house, and posing it at the dinner table or on the bed next to their sleeping widowed spouse hones the vampire's stealth and lockpickng skills, bonds the Pack in a frat-bro sort of way, and doesn't actually involve killing.<br /> <br /> That said, the Cammy predator types still don't work. While Sabbat aren't all psycho's, almost all the standard predator types assume someone actively attempting to retain their humanity.<br /> <br /> The one exception, Alleycat, still doesn't work because beating people up for food wouldn't cost you rating on most paths. So the flaw baked into it, losing a humanity point, doesn't work, and would need to be replaced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 03-28-2021, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T15:08:30-07:00","id":1441812,"title":"","content":"Paths are supposed to be harder than humanity. They are supposed to limit you vs being on humanity,. That they might have fewer Predator style options compared to humamity seems like a reasonable trade off. So the sabbat book might come new types for each Path but they would be much smaller in number. While Humanity could take just about anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T15:24:25-07:00","id":1441815,"title":"","content":"I think the really strange and sick things the Sabbat do are done only at rare times. Because they would attract vampire hunters like crazy and cause debilitating casualties to the sect. Even the &quot;normal&quot; hunting the Sabbat does is more higher profile than Camarilla vampires, so the Sabbat should already have a bad problem with hunters and a much higher rate of destruction. Not just independent hunters, but organized hunters like the Inquisition, Lupines, and other enemies. Archon coteries like the Wolfpack for one. I imagine truly outrageous Sabbat antics even attracts the Technocracy to wipe out that particular pack.<br /> <br /> As a result, while the Sabbat often talks about outrageous things that have been done, they don't really do them. That story about Sabbat hunting people in malls that every pack uproariously talks about? Yeah, it happened ONCE. And soon afterwards, the pack was never heard from again. What happened to them? Nobody knows. But hey, it's a cool story so it gets told a lot. So while the Sabbat all yuck it up as it proves how &quot;badass&quot; they are, every single one of them knows the real morale of that story - don't do stupid things like that or you'll get killed. <br /> <br /> And of course when you tell stories like that, they become embellished and become tall tales. Maybe that hunt at the &quot;mall&quot; was in fact just a gas station when someone's prey escaped and made their way there to call for help, and the pack was forced to deal with the people already there, and they had to make it look like a burglary gone bad. Much less impressive, so the story ends up changing over time. And tall tales can quickly diverge from one another. So that one incident leads to a dozen different stories that sound like separate events, but it still only happened once.<br /> <br /> And not all of the inhuman Paths of Enlightenment lead to horrendous murder scenes. Some are quite indifferent to it, and others are even hostile. Vampires on the Path of Honorable Accord likely don't treat mortals any worse than vampires on Humanity. Vampires on the Path of Night don't want to kill mortals - they want to fill them with dread of evil so they turn towards God for salvation. A lot of Paths fall into this area. In fact, there's probably a lot of conflict between packs who follow these kind of Paths, and those whose antics violate them. Such conflicts might not end up in open warfare given the Sabbat tents of freedom and loyalty, but there's probably other ways of handling them especially if one can argue that such an antic &quot;betrayed&quot; the Sabbat by revealing the sect to its enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T15:32:18-07:00","id":1441818,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind the vast majority of truly egregious stuff the Sabbat gets up to is done during an invasion specifically to force the Cam to spend resources on Masquerade cover ups and divert said resources from being used in the actual conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T15:39:24-07:00","id":1441819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1441815#post1441815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the really strange and sick things the Sabbat do are done only at rare times. Because they would attract vampire hunters like crazy and cause debilitating casualties to the sect..</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that why the sect is basically... &quot;Elders and Neonates&quot; and nothing inbetween? The Sabbat IS the the Meatgrinder sect. Those who survive are scary powerful<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T15:44:16-07:00","id":1441821,"title":"","content":"Again, while not even close to all Sabbat are maniacs, even the most subtle of Sabbat would need the Predator types altered. A Sabbat siren-predator isn't going to put up with a spurned lover or jealous partner making trouble, for example. That's the sort of thing you put up with because you want to keep your humanity more than you want to simply drain the uppity nuisance and drop her or him in a dumpster. So that baked in flaw would need replacing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T15:58:34-07:00","id":1441822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1441805#post1441805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an odd take on feeding, alley cat ambushes, kidnappings, blood games etc are fairly standard, and part of why Sabbat cities have insane murder rates.... Sure don't tear apart the mayor outside the town hall but round up an entire encampment of rough sleepers, make them fight, eat the losers and embrace the winners? That's some quality entertainment, or hunt someone you deem to be strong, spend hours or nights tracking them, and draining them at the end? Feral Heart is all aboard that idea...</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be the first time we've agreed! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> JK<br /> <br /> But couldn't resist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1441808#post1441808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every member of the Sabbat ritually killing on average a person about once a season gives you a high murder rate. Those Sabbat killing people every night or even once a week doesn't give you a high-murder rate, it makes your city a concentration camp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. But you have to make some concessions to the World of Darkness elements. Which is to say that Sabbat who don't engage in regular murder just are not the same sect described in the books.<br /> <br /> Unrealistic or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-28-2021, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T16:07:15-07:00","id":1441823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1441821#post1441821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, while not even close to all Sabbat are maniacs, even the most subtle of Sabbat would need the Predator types altered. A Sabbat siren-predator isn't going to put up with a spurned lover or jealous partner making trouble, for example. That's the sort of thing you put up with because you want to keep your humanity more than you want to simply drain the uppity nuisance and drop her or him in a dumpster. So that baked in flaw would need replacing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feeding is hard. Caine is a Farmer, not a hunter. Do you know all the shit we put up with for farming from uppity plants and animals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T16:23:06-07:00","id":1441824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1440062-v5-the-sabbat-thread?p=1441821#post1441821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, while not even close to all Sabbat are maniacs, even the most subtle of Sabbat would need the Predator types altered. A Sabbat siren-predator isn't going to put up with a spurned lover or jealou